illside below Knightshayes Court near Bolham. The town\\''s name derives from \"Twy-ford-ton,\" meaning \"the town on two fords\".'' -> ''Tiverton is a town at the confluence of the rivers Exe and Lowman in Devon, England, with human occupation dating to the Stone Age, evidenced by numerous flint tools found in the area [1]. Cranmore Castle is one of the largest enclosures in Devon at over 15 acres, with clear sightlines to other earthworks and overlooking the river confluence [2]. Its function remains debated -- possibly a livestock enclosure, market site, or tribal oppidum [2]. The town\\''s name derives from \"Twy-ford-ton,\" meaning \"the town on two fords\" [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245547", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245548", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346218", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346219", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:399511", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:399512", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start None -> ''1''"}]'::jsonb),
