    ('0415d29e-5239-40c6-ab1d-5b19e443336b'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:0415d29e-5239-40c6-ab1d-5b19e443336b:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''7'' restored on Odigitria', '9d4f7db6f32d9dd102320fbd92ede722', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Cemetery'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 11 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29652", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0320:chunk-0001: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:30333", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-22_mechanical-period-name: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:32995", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0011:chunk-0001: description ''Odigitria is a Minoan cemetery in the Asterousia mountains of southern Crete, near the Odigitria Monastery. The site contains two tholos tombs (A and B), a rectangular building, courtyards, an ossuary, and a possible altar enclosed within a peribolos wall. Dating from Early Minoan I to Middle Minoan IA, the tombs were in use for over 1,000 years, with three construction phases beginning in the Final Neolithic. Artifacts include seals, gold diadems, a gold bracelet, and 474 obsidian blades, most made specifically as grave goods. Bodies were initially interred in tholos tombs or pithoi before secondary transfer to the ossuary.'' -> ''Odigitria is the archaeological site of an ancient Minoan religious complex, which includes two tholos tombs located near the modern Odigitria Monastery in the Asterousia mountains of southern Crete [1]. The tombs are dated from Early Minoan I to Middle Minoan IA and were excavated in 1979 by N. Dimopoulou and in 1980 by Antonis Vasilakis [1]. They were in use for more than 1,000 years [1]. Artifacts found include seals, amulets, necklaces, gold diadems, stone blades, stone vases, pots and a gold bracelet [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35633", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35634", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: period_start ''-3000'' -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:113445", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:113446", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s001: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-3000''"}]'::jsonb),
