ious complex, which includes two tholos tombs located near the modern Odigitria Monastery in the Asterousia mountains of southern Crete [1]. The tombs are dated from Early Minoan I to Middle Minoan IA and were excavated in 1979 by N. Dimopoulou and in 1980 by Antonis Vasilakis [1]. They were in use for more than 1,000 years [1]. Artifacts found include seals, amulets, necklaces, gold diadems, stone blades, stone vases, pots and a gold bracelet [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35633", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35634", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: period_start ''-3000'' -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:113445", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:113446", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s001: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-3000''"}]'::jsonb),
