 evident, three within the fort and the remainder in a series of seven embanked enclosures outside it [1]. A field system delineated by rubble and boulder boundaries is found to the south and east of the enclosures [1]. A lacrymatory was discovered at the site in 1824, and a quern-stone in 1885 [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:113506", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s001: site_type ''Fortress/citadel'' -> ''Fort''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:113507", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s001: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jenny%27s_Lantern'' -> ''https://keystothepast.info/search-records/results-of-search/results-of-search-2/Site-Details/?PRN=N4380''"}]'::jsonb),
