ution. A large cemetery at Tower Hill contained both cremation and inhumation burials, along with high-status finds including lead coffins, bronze bowls, and a rare oculist''s stamp. Evidence of Saxon occupation was also discovered outside the town walls.\" -> ''Sandy was a significant Romano-British small town in Central Bedfordshire [1] [2]. Recent excavations uncovered the first Roman town wall found in Bedfordshire, built from local ironstone and mortar, enclosing an area of about 11 hectares [1] [3]. A large cemetery at Tower Hill contained both cremation and inhumation burials [4]. Evidence of Saxon occupation was also discovered outside the town walls [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245667", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245668", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-1500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346296", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346297", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('0b34fdec-f221-40f9-8238-2d78d7ce6638'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '2', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:0b34fdec-f221-40f9-8238-2d78d7ce6638:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''2'' restored on Cranon', '37943d63505ceb1a42d0562efbef935b', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''Undated'') is shared by 120 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33045", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0012:chunk-0001: description ''Cranon (Κραννών) was an ancient Greek polis (city-state) in the region of Pelasgiotis, Thessaly, Greece [1]. The settlement was situated southwest of Larissa at a distance of 100 stadia from Gyrton, as recorded by the geographer Strabo [1]. Cranon was bounded by the territory of Atrax to the west and Scotussa to the east, while the ridges of Revenia to the south separated it from the valley of the river Enipeus [1].'' -> ''Cranon or Crannon was a town and polis (city-state) of Pelasgiotis, in ancient Thessaly, situated southwest of Larissa, and at the distance of 100 stadia from Gyrton, according to Strabo [1]. After the Battle of Chaeronea (338 BCE), the Phocians fought in Lamia and in the Battle of Crannon against Antipater and his army [1]. This was the decisive battle of the Lamian War between Macedon and Athens with its allies [1]. In 191 BCE, Crannon was taken by Selecuid king Antiochus III [1]. The first epigraphic reference to the polis of the Cranionians is in an honorific decree of the 3rd century BCE [1]. At an indeterminate date Cranon was a walled and fortified city, but almost nothing is known about the urban centre and the acropolis, except for a possible temple of Athena Polias erected on it [1]. There were also temples of Aesclepius, Apollo, Poseidon and Zeus [1]. The city minted silver coins in the fifth century BCE (480-400 BCE) and bronze coins in the fourth century BCE [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93246", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93247", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: period_start ''-2000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245669", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:245670", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346298", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346299", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-3000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
