 above sea level. The fort covers about 2.2 acres, defended naturally by steep drops on two sides and by double banks and ditches on the south side. A late-1950s study by Nottingham University students revealed two distinct Iron Age construction phases: initially a dry-stone wall along the south side, later replaced by a ditch with inner bank and a new outer rampart faced with dry stone walling. Roman coins of Emperor Constantine and Romano-British pottery were found near a spring within the defences. A medieval packhorse track leads uphill into the fort, built to access the enclosed spring. It is a scheduled monument.'' -> ''Castle Naze is an Iron Age promontory hillfort occupying a triangular spur of Combs Edge in the Derbyshire Peak District [1] [2].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234560", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: lat ''53.28206624821575'' -> ''53.3027''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234561", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: lon ''-1.9313459873277'' -> ''-1.92102''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246033", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246034", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304786", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0bff4ef7/Castle Naze earthworks.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0bff4ef7/Castle_Naze_on_Combs_Moss.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:305987", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001-rollback-rest-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0bff4ef7/Castle_Naze_on_Combs_Moss.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0bff4ef7/Castle Naze earthworks.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:306872", "url": "remediation_chang