]. Research by A. H. A. Hogg on this hill fort was published in 1982 [1]. The course of a Roman road, Sarn Helen can be traced from south-west to north-east across the common [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:113533", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s001: lat ''51.928145522572784'' -> ''51.9417''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:113534", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s001: lon ''-3.490064375768906'' -> ''-3.4708''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:113535", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:113536", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s001: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:113537", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s001: site_type ''Fortress/citadel'' -> ''Fort''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:142808", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-002: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Mynydd_Illtud_Powys_Twyn_y_Gaer_HenSne_02_trig_point.JPG/400px-Mynydd_Illtud_Powys_Twyn_y_Gaer_HenSne_02_trig_point.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0c879c8d/Twyn_y_Gaer_iron_age_hill_fort_at_Mynydd_Illtud,_east_side.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246035", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246036", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:384970", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:384971", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_