ica''s most significant archaeological regions.\" -> ''An extensive pre-Columbian archaeological landscape spanning much of Beni Department, Bolivia [1]. The remains include over 4,700 artificial forest islands, monumental mounds, raised agricultural fields, canals, causeways, ring ditches, and fish weirs [1] [2]. The Casarabe Culture (500-1400 CE) constructed a dense settlement network of over 189 earthen mounds interconnected by causeways across at least 4,500 km2 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304833", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0ec71a0c/Pre-Columbian_man-made_causeway_in_Llanos_de_Moxos.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0ec71a0c/Beni_Department_aérea_25.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:306034", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-001-001-rollback-rest-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0ec71a0c/Beni_Department_aérea_25.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0ec71a0c/Pre-Columbian_man-made_causeway_in_Llanos_de_Moxos.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:306919", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0ec71a0c/Pre-Columbian_man-made_causeway_in_Llanos_de_Moxos.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0ec71a0c/Beni_Department_aérea_25.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('0ed79845-f651-4c52-85cd-7f96bab43d4e'::uuid, 'mystery', '8', '9', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:0ed79845-f651-4c52-85cd-7f96bab43d4e:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''9'' restored on Eightercua Stone Row', '810d9f69f2b7218d5cbcbf7bed6e7f9d', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 8 from (''Standing stone'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 3 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81828", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2044:chunk-0001: description ''Eightercua is a four-stone alignment megalithic tomb in County Kerry, Ireland, located 1.5 km south-south-east of Waterville. The tallest stone reaches 10 feet in height, with the alignment stretching 25 feet in an east-west direction [1][2]. Dating to circa 1700 BC, surrounding artifacts include remains of a possible tomb and ancient enclosure, suggesting ritual purpose [1][2]. By tradition, it is the burial place of Scéine, wife of Milesian leader Amergin mac Míled [1][2].'' -> ''Eightercua is thought to originate from around 1700 BC, and by tradition is the burial place of Scéine, wife of the leader of the Milesian invaders, Amergin mac Míled [1]. The site features four tall slabs from 1.8 to 3 meters high running east and west [1]. From one stone a slab runs south and could be part of a tomb chamber or cist set in an oval cairn 1 meter high [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:113564", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s001: site_type ''Megalithic stones'' -> ''Standing stone''"}, {"source": "remedi