gland [1] [2]. The site features a multiple stone row of at least 29.8 m with 15 stones in four rows aligned roughly NW-SE, and is a Scheduled Monument [3] [4]. Stone settings are the most common megalithic monuments on Exmoor, likely serving ceremonial or ritual purposes [5] [6].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234583", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234584", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-2350''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('0f42edd7-0a93-46bd-a65c-9382e076fac9'::uuid, 'mystery', '4', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:0f42edd7-0a93-46bd-a65c-9382e076fac9:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''5'' restored on Dedoplis Mindori', '7d3d26b9efb6fdfce8713ca9bfaa0c9a', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 4 from (''Temple complex'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 53 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:32777", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0005:chunk-0001: description \"2nd–1st c. BC religious complex at this multi-layer archaeological site in Shida Kartli, Georgia. Excavations have revealed Acheulean and Mousterian stone tools, Late Bronze to Iron Age burials, Classical Antiquity and Medieval settlements. The site''s religious buildings are listed as an Immovable Cultural Monument of National Significance.[1]\" -> \"Dedoplis Mindori is an archaeological site in Georgia''s east-central region of Shida Kartli, at the confluence of eastern and western Prone, tributaries of the Kura [1]. A multi-layer site, it has yielded some Acheulean and Mousterian stone tools, burials from the Late Bronze to the Iron ages, and several settlements and burials from the Classical Antiquity and Middle Ages [1]. Of particular importance is a substantial complex of what once were religious buildings, dated to the 2nd–1st century BC [1]. The excavations revealed an extensive complex of religious buildings at Dedoplis Mindori and a palace complex at Dedoplis Gora [1]. The complex consists of eight temples, two gateways, dwellings, and 