996, archaeological excavations uncovered objects that date to approximately 120,000-130,000 years ago, during the Paleolithic period [1]. If authentically dated, these artifacts would represent the only known Neanderthal presence in the Nordic countries [1].'' -> ''Wolf Cave (Finnish: Susiluola) is a natural cave formation at the border of Kristinestad and Karijoki municipalities in Finland [1] [2].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246061", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246062", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346320", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346321", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('0f4db519-d092-42de-b23c-0046c1db2fd2'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '2', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:0f4db519-d092-42de-b23c-0046c1db2fd2:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''2'' restored on Ancient City of Telmessos', '4a3aa598a50c7849ec83038cc7405bbe', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''Undated'') is shared by 120 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81866", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2045:chunk-0001: description \"Telmessos was the largest city in ancient Lycia, located near the modern town of Fethiye in southwestern Turkey[1]. The city flourished from approximately 1500 BC to 500 BC, situated on a peninsula with a well-protected harbor separated from the Gulf of Telmessos by a small island[1]. In the Lycian language, the city was known as Telebehi[1]. The site later became known as Anastasiopolis during the Byzantine period, and subsequently as Makri or Macre[1]. Telmessos was strategically positioned near the border between Lycia and Caria, and its maritime significance made it one of the most important coastal cities of ancient Lycia[1]. The ruins include ancient theaters, rock-cut tombs, and substantial architectural remains that testify to the city''s historical prominence[1].\" -> ''Telmessos or Telmessus, also Telmissus, later Anastasiopolis, then Makri or Macre, was the largest city in Lycia, near the Carian border [1]. The well-protected harbor of Telmessos is separated from the Gulf of Telmessos by an island [1]. The Hittite name was Kuwalapašša, while the Lycian name was Telebehi [1]. In the 13th century BC, the Annals of Hattusili III mentions the city as a part of Lukka and conquered by the Hittites [1]. Telmessos was a flourishing city in the west of Lycia, on the Gulf of Fethiye [1]. It was famed for its school of diviners, consulted among others by the Lydian king Croesus, prior to declaring war against Cyrus [1]. Telmessos was a member of the Delian League in the 5th century BC [1]. It was taken by Alexander the Great in 334 BC, when he came to the town after the siege of Halicarnassus [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93325", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:93326", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s002: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:142891", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0f4db519/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0f4db519/185A7357.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234585", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234586", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:331408", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-006-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/0f4db519/185A7357.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/0f4db519/Tomb of Amyntas.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345657", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345658", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
