 populations from the fallen cities of Ai-Khanoum and Takht-i Sangin resettled in the Jalalabad plains around Dionysopolis, contributing to the Greco-Buddhist art of nearby Hadda.'' -> ''Nagara, also known as Dionysopolis, was an ancient city in what is now eastern Afghanistan, associated with the site of Nagara Ghundi about 4 km west of Jalalabad near the junction of the Surkhab and Kabul rivers [1] [2]. Archaeologist Zemaryalai Tarzi proposed that Greek populations from the fallen cities of Ai-Khanoum and Takht-i Sangin resettled in the Jalalabad plains around Dionysopolis, contributing to the Greco-Buddhist art of nearby Hadda [1] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234592", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: lat ''34.43003080961005'' -> ''34.446552''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:234593", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s001: lon ''70.45879738028611'' -> ''70.397583''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246065", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246066", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345659", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345660", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''1'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
