tlements, later incorporating additional towns including Ithome according to Strabo [1] [2]. The city formed part of a strategic quadrangle with Tricca, Pelinnaeum, and Gomphi, and its location is confirmed by Julius Caesar''s march from Gomphi to Pharsalus in 48 BC during the Civil War [1] [2] [3] [4].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246129", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246130", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346372", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:346373", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-3000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('171c0658-fbad-43fd-9764-fa7b37c5ba28'::uuid, 'antiquity', '8', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:171c0658-fbad-43fd-9764-fa7b37c5ba28:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: antiquity ''5'' restored on Three Brothers of Grugith', 'ec987b40260fcd34f8598ebb1240afe8', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 8 from period_start -4500"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:82022", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2049:chunk-0001: description ''A Neolithic portal dolmen near St Keverne on the Lizard peninsula in Cornwall, dating to approximately 3500-2600 BC. Two parallel orthostats support a large capstone enclosing a chamber measuring about 4 by 2 metres. The capstone bears cupmarks that may represent early prehistoric rock art. Excavated by Borlase in 1872, who discovered a pit about 1 metre deep and a single flint flake. Local legend connects the three stones to a quarrel between St Keverne and St Just, in which the furious saint hurled the quarter-ton stones as weapons. The site is a scheduled monument overlooking Goonhilly Downs.'' -> ''The Three Brothers of Grugith is a prehistoric site, a dolmen of the Neolithic Age, near St Keverne in Cornwall, England [1]. It is a scheduled monument [1]. The dolmen is situated near the summit of a hill overlooking Goonhilly Downs [1]. Two orthostats support a capstone; there are depressions on the capstone which may be cup marks, or may be naturally formed [1]. The chamber enclosed by the stones measures about 4 by 2 metres (13.1 by 6.6 ft), height about 1 metre (3 ft 3 in) [1]. William Copeland Borlase excavated the chamber in 1872: he discovered a pit about 1 metre (3 ft 3 in) deep, and one flint flake [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94333", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94334", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94335", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: site_type ''Megalithic stones'' -> ''Dolmen''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:143475", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-003: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f5/The_Three_Brothers_of_Crugith_%28or_Grugwith%29_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1826904.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/171c0658/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246131", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246132", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:324957", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/171c0658/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/171c0658/The Three Brothers of Crugith (or Grugwith) - geograph.org.uk - 1826904.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:384990", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:384991", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:399567", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''Undated'