dy the region''s cultural landscape from the Bronze Age through the Classical period.\" -> \"Desfina is a town in southern Phocis, Greece [1]. The area has far older significance: on the hill of Kastrouli, a fortified Mycenaean settlement from the 13th-12th century BC features Cyclopean walls approximately 1.2-1.4 m wide, tentatively identified with Homeric Anemoreia [1] [2] [3]. The Southern Phokis Regional Project now conducts transdisciplinary research combining classics, archaeochemistry, and digital humanities to study the region''s cultural landscape [3].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246531", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246532", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347173", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347174", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
