western slope of Porth Hellick Down [1]. The burial monument is situated close to the boundary of a prehistoric field system [1]. The site was excavated by the antiquarian, George Bonsor in 1899 [1]. He named the entrance grave, \"The Great Tomb\" [1]. Earlier unrecorded excavations at the site had left the burial chamber empty, except for a piece of pumice and a few remnants of late Bronze Age pottery fragments [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94515", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: site_type ''Cairn'' -> ''Cemetery''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('1fa55186-ecc7-4af0-99bb-87436b1e77b0'::uuid, 'antiquity', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:1fa55186-ecc7-4af0-99bb-87436b1e77b0:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: antiquity ''5'' restored on Crug Hywel', '8a2106e9c3eb683185e8d72bbc0cc53a', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 6 from period_start -1500"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33229", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0017:chunk-0001: description ''Crug Hywel (c. 1500–500 BC) is an Iron Age Celtic hillfort in Powys, Wales, featuring a well-preserved earth and stone rampart and ditch system [1]. The flat-topped hill, also known as Table Mountain, rises prominently above the Usk Valley near Crickhowell [1]. The site is accessible via public footpaths from Crickhowell and Llanbedr, including the Beacons Way long-distance trail [1]. It lies within open access land under the Countryside and Rights of Way Act, allowing public roaming [1].'' -> ''Crug Hywel is an Iron Age Celtic hillfort, with a clearly visible earth and stone ditch and rampart [1]. The name is sometimes given to the flat-topped hill itself, which is also called Table Mountain in English [1]. Located at the southern edge of the Black Mountains in south-east Wales, it rises to 451 m above sea level, from the southern flank of Pen Cerrig-calch, and overlooks the town of Crickhowell, whose name derives from Crug Hywel [1]. The Welsh name Mynydd y Begwn is also used for this summit [1]. The hill is formed from Old Red Sandstone originating in the Devonian period, specifically the sandstones of the Brownstones Formation, topped by rocks of the Quartz Conglomerate Group [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94516", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:94517", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:144571", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-005: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/1fa55186/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/1fa55186/Crug_Hywel_Hill_Fort,_Near_Abergavenny.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246535", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246536", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s003: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385029", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385030", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:399599", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:399600", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start None -> ''-1500''"}]'::jsonb),
