    ('20364c84-1e5f-4324-ad5c-be3f0d31586d'::uuid, 'antiquity', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:20364c84-1e5f-4324-ad5c-be3f0d31586d:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: antiquity ''5'' restored on Kingsdown Camp', 'b5dee2f9a043fb306bb597a2dbffbe66', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 6 from period_start -1500"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:80708", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2005:chunk-0001: description ''Kingsdown Camp is an Iron Age univallate hillfort at Buckland Dinham, 4.5 km southeast of Radstock, Somerset. The roughly quadrilateral enclosure covers 0.15 ha and features a drystone wall possibly 4 m high and 2.5 m wide, with an entrance on the northeast side. Excavations in 1927-29 revealed Iron Age occupation from about 400 BC to AD 50, yielding pottery, currency bars, bone needles, and an iron dagger. The fort was reoccupied in the Roman period through the late 1st-2nd centuries AD, with a new paved entrance, Romano-British brooches, coins, iron slag from metalworking, and burials. It is a Scheduled Ancient Monument.'' -> ''Kingsdown Camp is an Iron Age hillfort at Buckland Dinham 4.5 kilometres South East of Radstock, Somerset [1]. It is a Scheduled Monument [1]. It is a univallate hillfort with an area of 0.15 hectares, and is approximately quadrilateral in shape [1]. In the Iron Age or Roman period a drystone wall was constructed, possibly 4 metres high and 2.5 metres wide [1]. There is an entrance on the northeast side [1]. The fort continued to be used by the Romans [1].''"}, {"sou