 Period [1]. The site is dominated by a palace structure, consisting of 13 rooms all with doors opening on a central courtyard [1]. Each room is likely to have served a different purpose, with evidence for ovens, grain storage and a furnace for glass-making found in separate areas [1]. A more typical house from the site is similar in its design, but smaller in area, with divided rooms averaging 3x2m [1]. In contrast with Western Europe, timber is not used in construction, with all houses being made from sun-dried mud brick and having stone foundations [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95296", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95297", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:144720", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-005: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/25ba654d/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/25ba654d/Al-Rabadha_Jar.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246913", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246914", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347208", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347209", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''1'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('264ac74e-f5bc-4b73-b28a-c2db99132c50'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '2', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:264ac74e-f5bc-4b73-b28a-c2db99132c50:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''2'' restored on Wednesbury', 'ac280d01e74fb39839683c677f22f779', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''Undated'') is shared by 120 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:82376", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2060:chunk-0001: description ''A market town in the West Midlands whose name derives from Old English meaning \"Woden\\''s Fort,\" one of the few English places named after a pre-Christian deity. Church Hill is believed to have hosted an Iron Age hillfort, and a large ditch excavated at St Mary\\''s Road in 2008 predating the early medieval period supports this interpretation. The fortification may have been reused by Aethelflaed, Lady of the Mercians, as an Anglo-Saxon burh in the early 10th century.'' -> ''Wednesbury is situated five miles southeast of Wolverhampton, three miles southwest of Walsall and seven miles northwest of Birmingham [1]. The substantial remains of a large ditch excavated in St Mary\\''s Road in 2008 has been interpreted as part of a hilltop enclosure and possibly the Iron Age hillfort long suspected on the site [1]. The first authenticated spelling of the name was Wodensbyri, written in an endorsement on the back of the copy of the will of Wulfric Spot, dated 1004 [1]. Wednesbury (\"Woden\\''s borough\") is one of a number of places in England to be named after the pre-Christian deity Woden, the leader of the Old English pantheon [1]. During the Anglo-Saxon period there are believed to have been two battles fought in Wednesbury, in 592 and 715 [1]. According to The Anglo-Saxon Chronicle there was \"a great slaughter\" in 592 and \"Ceawlin was driven out\" [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95307", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95308", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:144726", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-005: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/16/St_Bartholomew%27s_Wednesbury.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/264ac74e/Wednesbury_-_the_High_Street.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246919", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246920", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:308570", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/264ac74e/Wednesbury_-_the_High_Street.webp'' -> \"/data/images/wiki/264ac74e/St_Bartholomew''s_Wednesbury.webp\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347214", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347215", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
