]. In 1723 Henry Rowlands described them as part of a ruinous circle of eight stones, some 16 m across [1]. An account of 1797 says that \"ignorant country people supposing money was hid under them tore them up\" and today only two stones, one slab and one pillar, stand in a modern field bank [1]. Nothing else is visible on the ground, but a 2008 excavation found three pits of standing stones, two containing stone stumps, consistent with the record by Rowlands [1]. Further excavations in 2010 identified the pits of three more removed standing stones, making seven identified in all of the eight expected to make up the original circle [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95311", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95312", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246923", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246924", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:324976", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/26de5254/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/26de5254/Bryn Gwyn slab stone with small adult 11102009.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385045", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385046", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:399615", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name 