n the late 1st century, a Romano-British farmhouse was built within the abandoned prehistoric enclosure [1]. Excavations were carried out at Alfred''s Castle from 1998 to 2000 by archaeologists from Oxford University [1]. A final analysis was published in 2014 [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:145394", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/285feaf7/hero.webp'' -> \"/data/images/wiki/285feaf7/Alfred''s Castle - panoramio.webp\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:321241", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-004-001: thumbnail_url \"/data/images/wiki/285feaf7/Alfred''s Castle - panoramio.webp\" -> ''/data/images/wiki/285feaf7/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:324981", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/285feaf7/hero.webp'' -> \"/data/images/wiki/285feaf7/Alfred''s Castle, Oxfordshire, aerial view from North.webp\""}]'::jsonb),
