ated south of Lake Titicaca in Ingavi Province, the site at its peak covered approximately 17 acres and featured at least three sunken temples, multiple platforms, and a central plaza. Excavations between 2005-2007 uncovered 972 bone fragments from at least 25 individuals in a circular structure, revealing evidence of a mortuary ritual where specialists used heated caustic limewater to disarticulate and clean bones of the deceased before returning them to families.'' -> ''Qhunqhu Wankani (also known as Khonkho Wankane) is a ceremonial centre in Bolivia predating the rise of the nearby city of Tiwanaku [1] [2] [3]. Located south of Lake Titicaca in Ingavi Province, the site at its peak covered approximately 17 acres and featured at least three sunken temples, multiple platforms, and a central plaza [1] [3] [4]. Excavations between 2005-2007 uncovered 972 bone fragments from at least 25 individuals in a circular structure [3] [5].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235668", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: site_type None -> ''Temple complex''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('29d6fc00-4e39-4707-bea6-237454b055fb'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '2', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:29d6fc00-4e39-4707-bea6-237454b055fb:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''2'' restored on Lagina', 'e0ade1470cb3a5107083aa1b67bb041a', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''Undated'') is shared by 120 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29712", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0331:chunk-0001: site_type ''Megalithic stones'' -> ''Settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:82504", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2063:chunk-0001: description \"An ancient sanctuary in Caria (modern Turgut, southwestern Turkey) containing a monumental temple of Hecate built in the 2nd century BC, measuring 21.3 by 28 meters with Corinthian columns. The temple''s four sculpted friezes depict the Gigantomachy, Zeus''s birth, a Roman-Amazon pact, and a league of Carian cities, now housed in Istanbul''s Archaeological Museums. A sacred road connected Lagina to the city of Stratonicea 15 km away, along which annual pilgrimages and a Key-Carrying ceremony by young girls were conducted. First investigated by Charles Newton in 1856, and later excavated by Osman Hamdi Bey in 1891-1892; restoration efforts re-erected the ancient columns in 2020.\" -> ''Lagina or Laginia was a town and religious centre in ancient Caria [1]. It contained an important monumental temple of Hecate, at which great festivals were celebrated every year [1]. For most of antiquity, it was a part of the territory of Stratonicea [1]. Its site is located near Turgut, Anatolia [1]. Little is known about the early history of Lagina as a town and religious sanctuary, although it existed as early as the 4th century BCE [1]. Lagina became one of the major rural cult centres of the polis of Stratonicea [1]. The British archaeologist Charles Thomas Newton found over thirty inscriptions and nine decorated frieze blocks at the site in 1856 [1]. Authorised excavations began at Lagina in 1891 under the direction of Osman Hamdi Bey [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95388", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:95389", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:145443", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/29d6fc00/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/29d6fc00/The Sanctuary of Hecate in Lagina, Caria, Turkey (17082040067).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235671", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:235672", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s002: period_start None -> ''-400''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:331535", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-006-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/29d6fc00/The Sanctuary of Hecate in Lagina, Caria, Turkey (17082040067).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/29d6fc00/The Sanctuary of Hecate in Lagina, Caria, Turkey (17263493936).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347246", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347247", "url": "remedi