[1]. The whole burial chamber was once covered by a mound of earth or stones and once these were removed stones were used to block the holes in the sides of the tomb so that it could be used as a shelter for sheep [1]. The site was excavated in 1968 which revealed four additional stone-holes, one having supported a further chamber stone, the others indicating a possible passage leading off to the northwest [1]. Slight traces of a covering cairn were found to the south and it was shown that the monument had been raised over a pit 0.8 metres deep, filled with clay and stones [1]. Finds included a small quantity of burnt bone, pottery, and flints [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96295", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96296", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:145482", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2adae6b7/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2adae6b7/Carreg_Samson,_Sir_Benfro_in_2021_13.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246969", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246970", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:308674", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2adae6b7/Carreg_Samson,_Sir_Benfro_in_2021_13.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2adae6b7/Carreg_Samson,_Sir_Benfro_in_2021_08.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385058", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "reme