ne flour production via spinning wheels or natural erosion from glacial meltwater.'' -> ''Sliprannor i Gantofta is a sandstone outcrop near Helsingborg in Scania, Sweden, covered with grooves along the Raa river valley escarpment [1] [2]. Once thought to be marks from sharpening weapons, modern scholars have disproven this theory [3] [4]. Other hypotheses propose stone flour production [3] [5].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246991", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246992", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-10000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:308713", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2d12562b/Grooves Gantofta 1.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2d12562b/Sliprännor_Gantofta_2.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347277", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347278", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-10000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
