icance. Other hypotheses propose stone flour production via spinning wheels or natural erosion from glacial meltwater.'' -> ''Sliprannor i Gantofta is a sandstone outcrop near Helsingborg in Scania, Sweden, covered with grooves along the Raa river valley escarpment [1] [2]. Once thought to be marks from sharpening weapons, modern scholars have disproven this theory [3] [4]. Other hypotheses propose stone flour production [3] [5].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246991", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:246992", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-10000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:308713", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2d12562b/Grooves Gantofta 1.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/2d12562b/Sliprännor_Gantofta_2.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347277", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:347278", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s002: period_start ''-10000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('2d48d802-42b6-4d45-95ac-54edd7eece15'::uuid, 'antiquity', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:2d48d802-42b6-4d45-95ac-54edd7eece15:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: antiquity ''5'' restored on Largin Castle', '95ace56b8ee86f03f13e6b31dd46ee3a', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 6 from period_start -1500"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33535", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0021:chunk-0001: description ''Largin Castle is a large multivallate Iron Age hillfort in East Cornwall, sitting atop a steep ridge above the River Fowey valley at 130 metres elevation. Covering approximately 1.8 hectares, the site features triple ramparts and ditches surrounding an oval central enclosure, with ramparts reaching as much as 3.5 metres high in places. A Bronze Age urn of the local Trevisker style discovered in 1975 suggests earlier occupation predating the hillfort. Despite being described by Historic England as \"arguably of national importance,\" the site was not scheduled as a monument until June 2020 and very little archaeological study has been conducted.'' -> ''Largin Castle is a contour hillfort and scheduled monument in Cornwall presumed to date from the Iron Age [1]. Largin Castle is situated approximately 4.5 kilometres west of Dobwalls, on a hill spur above the north-facing southern slope of the Fowey valley, at an elevation of 130 meters above sea level [1]. It is described in the Atlas of Hillforts of Britain and Ireland as having a complex shape occupying an area of 1.8 hectares [1]. The hillfort has an outer rampart and ditch enclosure with an entrance at its south [1]. Within this, a smaller inner oval enclosure, also defined by ramparts and ditch, is offset to the north and occupies some 3/4 of the interior [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96328", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96329", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:145619", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/2d48d802/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247329", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247330", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385064", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385065", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:399633", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:399634", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start None -> ''-1500''"}]'::jsonb),
