    ('31ee7df0-cf14-4c97-8d88-697625e5b913'::uuid, 'mystery', '4', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:31ee7df0-cf14-4c97-8d88-697625e5b913:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''5'' restored on Chanquillo', '761b54852404b3b85a9f738756f071d6', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 4 from (''Temple complex'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 53 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44119", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0088:chunk-0001: description \"Chankillo is an ancient monumental complex in Peru''s coastal desert, located in the Casma-Sechin basin of Áncash Department. The ruins include a hilltop fort, thirteen stone towers forming a solar observatory dating to the 3rd century BC, and residential and gathering areas [1]. The Thirteen Towers represent one of the oldest known astronomical observatories in the Americas, used to track solar alignments throughout the year [1]. The site was constructed by the Casma/Sechin culture (Sechin Complex) and earned UNESCO World Heritage status in July 2021 [1].\" -> ''Chankillo is an ancient monumental complex in the Peruvian coastal desert, found in the Casma-Sechin basin in the Áncash Department of Peru [1]. The ruins include the hilltop Chankillo fort, the nearby Thirteen Towers solar observatory, and residential and gathering areas [1]. The Thirteen Towers have been interpreted as an astronomical observatory built in the third century BC [1]. The culture that produced Chankillo is called the Casma/Sechin culture or the Sechin Complex [1]. The site covers about four square kilometres and has been interpreted as a fortified temple [1]. The regularly-spaced thirteen towers of Chankillo were constructed atop the ridge of a low hill running near north to south, forming a \"toothed\" horizon with narrow gaps at regular intervals [1]. The Thirteen Towers of Chankillo could be the earliest known observatory in the Americas [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:114981", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s002: site_type ''Fortress/citadel'' -> ''Temple complex''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:333728", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-001: thumbnail_url \"/data/images/wiki/31ee7df0/241 of ''Peru- incidents of ravel and exploration in the Land of the Incas. ... With illustrations'' (11265556566).webp\" -> ''/data/images/wiki/31ee7df0/Chanquillo_Fortaleza_(remains).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
