Sechin Complex [1]. The site covers about four square kilometres and has been interpreted as a fortified temple [1]. The regularly-spaced thirteen towers of Chankillo were constructed atop the ridge of a low hill running near north to south, forming a \"toothed\" horizon with narrow gaps at regular intervals [1]. The Thirteen Towers of Chankillo could be the earliest known observatory in the Americas [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:114981", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s002: site_type ''Fortress/citadel'' -> ''Temple complex''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:333728", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-001: thumbnail_url \"/data/images/wiki/31ee7df0/241 of ''Peru- incidents of ravel and exploration in the Land of the Incas. ... With illustrations'' (11265556566).webp\" -> ''/data/images/wiki/31ee7df0/Chanquillo_Fortaleza_(remains).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
