h and bank are separated by a berm, which was originally 5 metres wide [1]. It encloses an area 53 by 46 metres, with entrances to the north and south, each of which have a causeway across the ditch [1]. A minor excavation was carried out in the west ditch in 1902 by Micah Salt; this reputedly discovered some pottery sherds and flint flakes, which have since been lost [1]. A trial excavation by Oxford University Archaeological Society in 1949 established that the ring has two entrances, and also provided information about the original size of the bank and ditch [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96444", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96445", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:146329", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-007: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/75/BullRingDoveHoles.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/31efd673/The Bull Ring Henge 3.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247383", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247384", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309394", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/31efd673/The Bull Ring Henge 3.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/31efd673/BullRingDoveHoles.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385081", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385082", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-per