e Cave of Maltravieso in Caceres, Extremadura, was discovered in 1951 when a quarry explosion exposed the cavity [1] [2]. It contains 71 hand stencils created by blowing pigment around hands placed on the walls, along with linear designs and animal paintings [1] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247387", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247388", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s005: period_start None -> ''-10000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309406", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/32a2b3eb/Cueva de Maltravieso 01.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/32a2b3eb/EntradaMaltravieso.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385085", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385086", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start ''-10000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:399651", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:399652", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start None -> ''-4501''"}]'::jsonb),
