uddha [1]. Modern restoration accounts for their order in the Lahore Museum [1]. Three photos taken around 1890 show the order of the panels in the earliest restoration [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:96472", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s005: site_type ''Temple complex'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:146360", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-007: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/43/Stupa_-_Lahore_Museum.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/33ac2b60/Buddhist Carved Stone and Budha Statue.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309432", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/33ac2b60/Buddhist Carved Stone and Budha Statue.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/33ac2b60/Stupa_-_Lahore_Museum.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
