    ('349e080c-0b4f-4708-8744-d1b1c6a0b83e'::uuid, 'mystery', '4', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:349e080c-0b4f-4708-8744-d1b1c6a0b83e:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''5'' restored on Temple of Zeus, Olympia', '288a2d8398342d0f814be46850ec32d2', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 4 from (''Temple complex'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 53 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29690", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0326:chunk-0001: period_start ''-1500'' -> ''-472''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:30378", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-22_mechanical-period-name: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:33587", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0022:chunk-0001: description ''The Temple of Zeus at Olympia, designed by architect Libon of Elis, was built between 470 and 456 BC as the quintessential Doric order Greek temple. It featured six columns across its front, thirteen along each side, and was constructed from local shell-conglomerate covered in white stucco. Inside stood the chryselephantine Statue of Zeus by Phidias, nearly 12 metres tall and counted among the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World. The pediments depicted the chariot race of Pelops and the battle of Lapiths and Centaurs, while metopes illustrated the Twelve Labours of Heracles. Emperor Theodosius II ordered its burning in 426 AD, and earthquakes in 551-552 AD toppled the remains.'' -> ''The Temple of Zeus was an ancient Greek temple in Olympia, Greece, dedicated to the god Zeus [1]. The temple, built in the second quarter of the fifth century BC, was the very model of the fully developed classical Greek temple of the Doric order [1]. The temple was constructed between c.\\u2009472 and 456 BC [1]. The building sat on a crepidoma (platform) of three unequal steps, the exterior columns were positioned in a six by thirteen arrangement, two rows of seven columns divided the cella (inner chamber) into three aisles [1]. The Eastern pediment depicts the chariot race between Pelops and Oenomaus, while the Western pediment features a Centauromachy with Theseus and the Lapiths [1]. The metopes from the temple depict the twelve labours of Heracles [1]. The temple housed the renowned Statue of Zeus, which was one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World [1]. The chryselephantine (gold and ivory) statue was approximately 13 m (43 ft) high, and was made by the sculptor Phidias in his workshop on the site at Olympia [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:146374", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-007: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/27/Dias_entrance_EAST_01.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/349e080c/20190506 214 olympia.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309444", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/349e080c/20190506 214 olympia.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/349e080c/Dias_entrance_EAST_01.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
