    ('379931c0-89c4-4e2a-9c73-ec2472542070'::uuid, 'mystery', '1', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:379931c0-89c4-4e2a-9c73-ec2472542070:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''4'' restored on Dun Ringill', '5e81758982e56bb3565e8dada21252c1', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 1 from (''Fortress/citadel'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 235 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:80788", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2008:chunk-0001: description ''Dun Ringill is an Iron Age hill fort on the Strathaird peninsula on the island of Skye, Scotland [1]. Further fortified in the Middle Ages, tradition holds that it was for several centuries the seat of Clan MacKinnon [1]. It is located east of Kirkibost on the west shore of Loch Slapin [1].'' -> ''Dun Ringill is an Iron Age hill fort on the Strathaird peninsula on the island of Skye, Scotland [1]. The original structure of Dun Ringill is consistent with an Iron Age broch dating to approximately the first years of the common era [1]. Dun Ringill today is a stacked stone ruin overlooking Loch Slapin [1]. The present structure is approximately 4 metres in height and 16 m on each side, with a ditch following the outer wall [1]. Its most notable feature is the central landward facing doorway approximately 1.8 m high that leads into the center of the structure [1]. The interior of the structure contained two rectangular buildings measuring 4.5 by 2.4 m [1]. The original layout was similar to that of a broch, a form of complex Atlantic roundhouse [1].''"}