    ('37d8c068-dfb3-4fc5-a99e-a09c4aad18d3'::uuid, 'mystery', '8', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:37d8c068-dfb3-4fc5-a99e-a09c4aad18d3:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''7'' restored on Susupillo', 'f6bce93280bd19d2cf7e9a4f1d18ffdb', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 8 from (''Castle/palace'', ''Undated'') is shared by 4 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:82804", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2072:chunk-0001: description ''Susupillo is an archaeological site on the northern slope of Susupillo mountain in the Andes of Peru, at over 3,800 m elevation in the Tantamayo District of Huanuco Region. The mountain itself rises to approximately 4,400 m. The site is part of the Tantamayo archaeological complex, which contains more than 80 sites featuring immense stone buildings up to 11 m high with as many as 6 stories, surrounded by formidable defensive walls. Susupillo was declared a National Cultural Heritage of Peru on June 18, 2002.'' -> ''Susupillo is a mountain with an archaeological site of the same name in the Andes of Peru, about 4,400 metres high [1]. It is situated in the Huánuco Region, Huamalíes Province, Tantamayo District [1]. The archaeological site of Susupillo lies on the northern slope of the mountain at about 9°23′32.4″S 76°41′33.5″W, at a height of more than 3,800 metres [1]. It was declared a National Cultural Heritage of Peru by Resolución Directoral No. 533/INC on June 18, 2002 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116182", "url": "remediation_change_log", "q