    ('3af2d2bf-8e21-4e12-83a7-5b1bffc3d5db'::uuid, 'antiquity', '7', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:3af2d2bf-8e21-4e12-83a7-5b1bffc3d5db:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: antiquity ''5'' restored on Huntersquoy Chambered Cairn', '2c75206f0a9d56c83f94ef6680b85fac', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 7 from period_start -3000"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:91860", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2211:chunk-0001: description ''Huntersquoy Chambered Cairn is a Neolithic chambered cairn on the island of Eday in Orkney, Scotland [1]. It is an Orkney-Cromarty type chambered cairn [1]. The monument is distinctive for its rare two-story design with overlapping chambers [1]. The site was designated a scheduled monument by Historic Environment Scotland in 1936 [1].'' -> ''Huntersquoy chambered cairn is a Neolithic chambered cairn located on the island of Eday, in Orkney [1]. Huntersquoy chambered cairn is situated on a gently sloping hill overlooking Calf Sound in Orkney, Scotland [1]. It is a good example of an Orkney–Cromarty chambered cairn [1]. It dates from the Neolithic era, sometime during the years 3000 through 2001 BC [1]. These tombs, often called \"stalled cairns\" are characterized by a central passage edged by upright stones which divide spaces into separate chambers [1]. Huntersquoy is unique in that it is a rare double-storied burial monument [1]. It is seen as a small, unobtrusive, circular mound, 10 m in diameter and 60 cm in height above ground [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:972