 [1]. Parts of Asseria''s city walls have survived, as well as a triumphal arch erected in 113 AD during the time of Trajan [1]. The city walls are of ashlar, predating Roman occupation [1]. Excavations have uncovered the 1st-century Roman forum, as well as a likely basilica [1]. Water was supplied by a 3 km-long aqueduct from the spring of Čatrnja in the village of Lisičić [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97294", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s006: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97295", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s006: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:147206", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-008: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/3d5420dd/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/3d5420dd/Ancient Asseria (ancient settlement in Croatia) 01.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247819", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247820", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_start None -> ''1''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:309598", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-004: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/3d5420dd/Ancient Asseria (ancient settlement in Croatia) 01.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/3d5420dd/Asseria,_Dalmatia_(12265922074).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348118", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348119", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:355625", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-24_mechanical-site-type-merge-s001: site_type ''Settlemen