arying in height from 0.8 metres to 2.1 metres [1]. The stones are irregularly spaced and aligned in a north easterly direction [1]. They are aligned towards a stone known as the Fiddler, which lies on the moorland approximately 800 metres away [1]. The stone row was first noted by historian Richard Carew in 1605 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97978", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s007: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97979", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s007: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:147812", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-009: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4b/Nine_maiden_jpg.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/402f38a8/The Nine Maidens Standing Stones (or five of them anyway^) - panoramio.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247861", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247862", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:333763", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/402f38a8/The Nine Maidens Standing Stones (or five of them anyway^) - panoramio.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/402f38a8/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348153", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348154", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2900''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:384195", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4400:chunk-0001: description 