    ('417445b4-e0db-49ac-99db-fe236794e9ff'::uuid, 'mystery', '4', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:417445b4-e0db-49ac-99db-fe236794e9ff:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''5'' restored on Parthenon', '226a7ba59e32a27fbacad048d05bbefe', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 4 from (''Temple complex'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 53 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:32815", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0009:chunk-0001: description ''The Parthenon, built 447-432 BC on the Athenian Acropolis, is a former temple dedicated to the goddess Athena. Designed by architects Ictinus and Callicrates under the supervision of sculptor Phidias, it used approximately 100,000 tons of Pentelic marble. Over its 2,500-year history it served as a Greek temple, Byzantine church, Catholic cathedral, Ottoman mosque, and ammunition store. A 1687 explosion left it in ruins. A UNESCO World Heritage Site, it remains one of the most iconic symbols of Ancient Greece and Western civilization.'' -> ''The Parthenon is a former temple on the Athenian Acropolis that was dedicated to the goddess Athena [1]. The Parthenon was built in the 5th century BC in thanksgiving for the Greek victory over the Persian invaders during the Greco-Persian Wars [1]. Construction started in 447 BC when the Delian League was at the peak of its power [1]. In the Morean War, a Venetian bomb landed on the Parthenon, which the Ottomans had used as a munitions dump, during the 1687 siege of the Acropolis [1]. The resulting explosion severely damaged the Parthenon [1]. The Parthenon was built under the general supervision of Phidias, who also had charge of the sculptural decoration [1]. The Parthenon is an octastyle peripteral Doric temple with an Ionic hexastyle amphiprostyle two-chambered cella [1]. The cella of the Parthenon housed the chryselephantine statue of Athena Parthenos sculpted by Phidias and dedicated in 439 or 438 BC [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:147852", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-009: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/03/The_East_Facade_pf_the_Parthenon_on_March_22%2C_2021.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/417445b4/The_East_Facade_of_the_Parthenon_on_March_22,_2021.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:333283", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-007-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/417445b4/The_East_Facade_of_the_Parthenon_on_March_22,_2021.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/417445b4/The East Facade pf the Parthenon on March 22, 2021.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:333298", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-008-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/417445b4/The East Facade pf the Parthenon on March 22, 2021.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/417445b4/The_East_Facade_of_the_Parthenon_on_March_22,_2021.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
