ge defended settlement, surrounded by a bank and ditch, lie south of Manor Farm. Excavations at Tower House Farm (1950-53) uncovered a Roman villa, and additional Roman features are scattered throughout the valley. The village also preserves earthworks from a deserted medieval settlement east of Wraxall House, with evidence of houses, enclosures, and possibly a watermill. The name Wraxall is thought to derive from ''a nook of land frequented by buzzards''.\" -> \"Wraxall is a village in North Somerset with archaeological heritage spanning multiple periods [1] [2]. Earthworks of an oval Iron Age settlement, surrounded by a bank and ditch, lie south of Manor Farm [1] [3]. Excavations (1950-53) uncovered a Roman villa, and additional Roman features are scattered throughout the valley [1] [2]. The village also preserves earthworks from a deserted medieval settlement, with evidence of houses, enclosures, and possibly a watermill [1]. The name Wraxall is thought to derive from ''a nook of land frequented by buzzards'' [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348159", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348160", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('418f6d87-0fc3-4eb6-a310-e45a1fb43a3d'::uuid, 'mystery', '4', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:418f6d87-0fc3-4eb6-a310-e45a1fb43a3d:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''5'' restored on Asclepieion of Pergamon', 'daf9a1afd8a073eeadfaeb0e5f6f76c5', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 4 from (''Temple complex'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 53 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:83394", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2079:chunk-0001: description \"One of antiquity''s foremost healing centres, rivalling Epidaurus and Kos, located 3 km southwest of the Pergamon acropolis in modern Bergama, Turkey. Founded in the 4th century BC, the complex featured a circular treatment centre with six apses, a 3,500-seat theatre, sacred spring, and underground passage. Patients received mud baths, massage, herbal treatments, and dream incubation therapy. The physician Galen, born in Pergamon in 129 AD, began his medical studies here at age 16. A colonnaded Via Tecta stretching 820 m led pilgrims to the sanctuary.\" -> \"The Asclepieion of Pergamon was an asclepieion, a healing temple, built in honour of the gods Asclepius and Hygieia, located west of the Pergamon hill, roughly three kilometers southwest of the acropolis in modern-day Bergama [1]. Founded in the mid-4th century BCE, it functioned as a religious and therapeutic centre through the Hellenistic and Roman periods, reaching its greatest prominence in the 2nd Century CE [1]. The Asclepieion grew across several distinct building phases spanning roughly eight centuries [1]. The sanctuary''s origins date to the mid-4th century BCE, when the complex consisted of a modest sacred enclosure and spring shrine at the site [1]. Under the Attalid dynasty in the 3rd and 2nd centuries BCE, the sanctuary saw its major expansion [1]. During this period, a Doric temple to Hygieia was built, along with a cluster of structures around the incubation area [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97999", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s007: source_url ''http://www.my-favourite-planet.de/english/middle-east/turkey/pergamon/pergamon-photos-01-035.html'' -> ''https://turkisharchaeonews.net/site/asclepieion-pergamon''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:147856", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-009: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/418f6d87/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/418f6d87/Asclepeion Ruins 醫廟遺址 - panoramio.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
