al distinct building phases spanning roughly eight centuries [1]. The sanctuary''s origins date to the mid-4th century BCE, when the complex consisted of a modest sacred enclosure and spring shrine at the site [1]. Under the Attalid dynasty in the 3rd and 2nd centuries BCE, the sanctuary saw its major expansion [1]. During this period, a Doric temple to Hygieia was built, along with a cluster of structures around the incubation area [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:97999", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s007: source_url ''http://www.my-favourite-planet.de/english/middle-east/turkey/pergamon/pergamon-photos-01-035.html'' -> ''https://turkisharchaeonews.net/site/asclepieion-pergamon''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:147856", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-009: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/418f6d87/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/418f6d87/Asclepeion Ruins 醫廟遺址 - panoramio.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('41eb7a6d-7eb0-4842-b25a-52cca7b3355e'::uuid, 'antiquity', '8', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:41eb7a6d-7eb0-4842-b25a-52cca7b3355e:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: antiquity ''5'' restored on Tŷ Newydd Burial Chamber', 'c5330f21a77d06a22e02c42cdaa0638d', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 8 from period_start -4500"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:34369", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0026:chunk-0001: description ''Tŷ Newydd Burial Chamber is a Neolithic dolmen dating to before 4500 BC, situated on a natural outcrop northeast of Llanfaelog on the Isle of Anglesey, Wales, near Tŷ Newydd farm [1]. The monument, now ruined, originally stood beneath a mound or cairn and is in the care of the Welsh historic environment service Cadw [1]. Its massive capstone measures 4 by 1.8 metres and is up to 1.2 metres thick, cracked and resting on three supporting stones [2].'' -> ''Tŷ Newydd Burial Chamber is a Neolithic dolmen located northeast of the village of Llanfaelog on the Isle of Anglesey in Wales [1]. Tŷ Newydd burial chamber is a ruined megalithic dolmen set up on a natural outcrop and would originally have been covered with a mound or cairn [1]. The capstone measures 4.0 metres by 1.8 metres and is up to 1.2 metres thick [1]. The capstone is cracked and rests on three of the four remaining uprights [1]. The chamber was excavated in August 1935 by Charles Phillips [1]. The chamber was found to be about 2.8 metres by 1.2 metres, and its area was defined by a spread of charcoal with a hearth at the eastern end, where there was thought to have been a second chamber or passage [1]. The finds included five flint flakes, a burnt flint arrowhead, a small chip from a polished flint axe, and nine small fragments of pottery [1]. Phillips believed that the pottery fragments were from the Beaker culture, and thus might represent Bronze Age reuse of an earlier Neolithic monument [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:83078", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26c_fields-wd1-s001: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:83079", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26c_fields-wd1-s001: period_start ''-5000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:147877", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-009: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8f/TyNewydd.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/41eb7a6d/Cromlech in Llanfaelog, Anglesey.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247875", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247876", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:333769", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/41eb7a6d/Cromlech in Llanfaelog, Anglesey.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/41eb7a6d/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385725", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385726", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:399693", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''Undated''