    ('432ee39e-5971-4c7e-a0a0-71684a7d3e0e'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:432ee39e-5971-4c7e-a0a0-71684a7d3e0e:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''7'' restored on Almendres Cromlech', '645de3fb8c04e6ac0d2c991a79956bb2', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Megalithic stones'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 12 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:34375", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0026:chunk-0001: description ''The Cromlech of the Almendres is a megalithic complex in the municipality of Évora, Alentejo, Portugal, located 4.5 km WSW of Nossa Senhora de Guadalupe village [1]. It is the largest existing group of structured menhirs in the Iberian Peninsula [1]. The site consists of several megalithic structures including cromlechs and menhir stones belonging to the \"Megalithic Universe of Évora\", with clear parallels to other cromlechs in the Évora District such as Portela Mogos and Vale Maria do Meio Cromlech [1].'' -> ''The Cromlech of the Almendres is a megalithic complex (commonly known as the Almendres Cromlech), located 4.5 road km WSW of the village of Nossa Senhora de Guadalupe, in the civil parish of Nossa Senhora da Tourega e Nossa Senhora de Guadalupe, municipality of Évora, in the Portuguese Alentejo [1]. The excavation of the site unearthed a series of both megalithic and neolithic construction phases; Almendres I 6000 BC, Almendres II 5000 BC, and Almendres III 4000 BC [1]. The complex, organized in a circular pattern, is marked by a forest of about 95 granite monoliths, deposited in small groups [1]. The older monoliths are formed as two or three concentric circles of smaller monoliths in the western part of the complex, while the Middle Neolithic structures consist of two ellipses (irregular but concentric) and large menhirs [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:147892", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-009: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/432ee39e/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/432ee39e/31096 Almendres Cromlech (55053696655).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:310292", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-005: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/432ee39e/31096 Almendres Cromlech (55053696655).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/432ee39e/Cromeleque_dos_Almendres1341.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
