cular pattern, is marked by a forest of about 95 granite monoliths, deposited in small groups [1]. The older monoliths are formed as two or three concentric circles of smaller monoliths in the western part of the complex, while the Middle Neolithic structures consist of two ellipses (irregular but concentric) and large menhirs [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:147892", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-009: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/432ee39e/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/432ee39e/31096 Almendres Cromlech (55053696655).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:310292", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-005: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/432ee39e/31096 Almendres Cromlech (55053696655).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/432ee39e/Cromeleque_dos_Almendres1341.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
