trance on the south-west, where two further banks create a barbican and where there is also a small area of chevaux de frise: sharp stones set on end, of which about 30 remain [1]. Craig Gwrtheyrn, or Caer Gwrtheyrn, is associated with the 5th-century British warlord Vortigern [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98037", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s007: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98038", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s007: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247885", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247886", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385729", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385730", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:399695", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:399696", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_start None -> ''-1500''"}]'::jsonb),
