 2012 [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98041", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s007: period_name ''500 - 1000 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98042", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s007: period_start ''500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247889", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_name None -> ''500 - 1000 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247890", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_start None -> ''500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348172", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''500 - 1000 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348173", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:384197", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4400:chunk-0001: description \"Tortuguero (or El Tortuguero) is an archaeological site in southernmost Tabasco, Mexico which supported a Maya city during the Classic period [1]. The site is noteworthy for its use of the B''aakal emblem glyph also found as the primary title at Palenque [1]. Because of its mid-20th century destruction, little is known about the dynastic lineage of this site [1]. Its history is linked to that of the kingdom of Palenque, as the rulers of Tortuguero used the same emblem glyph as Palenque [1]. Monument 6 from Tortuguero has recently generated discussion as it includes the only known inscription depicting the end of the current 13-Bak''tun era in 2012 [1].\" -> \"The site is noteworthy for its use of the B''aakal emblem glyph also found as the primary title at Palenque [1] [2].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:399697", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s001: period_name ''Und