g in festivities on a holy day [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98043", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s007: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98044", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s007: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247891", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247892", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348174", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348175", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('454b824c-cc1a-4846-97d8-7c036712895b'::uuid, 'antiquity', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:454b824c-cc1a-4846-97d8-7c036712895b:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: antiquity ''5'' restored on Y Garn Goch', 'e5860d33496272fb0d1551db72e804ae', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 6 from period_start -1500"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44329", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0090:chunk-0001: description ''Y Garn Goch is one of the largest hillforts in Wales, enclosing 16.6 hectares near the village of Bethlehem in the Brecon Beacons. The site comprises two Iron Age hillforts, Y Gaer Fawr and Y Gaer Fach, ringed by approximately 1,700 metres of stone ramparts with at least eight entrances and two prehistoric main gates featuring slab-lined passages. A 55-metre Neolithic stone long cairn crowns the highest summit, suggesting the site may incorporate earlier monuments. Recent research proposes it served ceremonial rather than purely military purposes, hosting equinox and solstice events.'' -> \"Y Garn Goch is a hill in the Brecon Beacons National Park in the east of Carmarthenshire, Wales [1]. The name means the ''red cairn'' [1]. It lies near the village of Bethlehem, three miles southwest of Llangadog and four miles east of Llandeilo on the southern side of the broad Towy Valley [1]. It is also commonly known as either Garn Goch or Carn Goch [1]. The established view is that Y Garn Goch is notable for the two impressive Iron Age hillforts of Y Gaer Fawr, (English: the big fort) and Y Gaer Fach, (English: the little fort), together the largest in southern Wales [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116322", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116323", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116324", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: site_type ''Fortress/citadel'' -> ''Fort''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:116325", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s003: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Y_Garn_Goch'' -> ''https://cy.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bryngaerau_Garn_Goch''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:148496", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-010: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/19/Y_Garn_Coch_fort.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/454b824c/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247893", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:247894", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s006: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:325014", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/454b824c/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/454b824c/Y Garn Coch fort.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385731", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385732", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:399699", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c