    ('4c6645cc-de9a-4a21-b932-809f7600337c'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:4c6645cc-de9a-4a21-b932-809f7600337c:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''4'' restored on Berry Head', '43085336a4cd673407742824304015ea', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Fort'', ''Undated'') is shared by 25 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44355", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0091:chunk-0001: description \"Berry Head is a limestone headland forming the southern boundary of Tor Bay near Brixham, Devon, fortified since the Iron Age as a promontory fort. An 18th-century observer recorded a cross-promontory rampart approximately 18 feet high before Napoleonic construction largely destroyed the prehistoric earthworks between 1794 and 1804. The Napoleonic fortifications, built to protect Torbay''s naval anchorage from French invasion, are among the most complete surviving examples in south-west England. The site includes two Scheduled Monuments, eight Listed Buildings, and is now a National Nature Reserve and SSSI managed by the Torbay Coast and Countryside Trust.\" -> ''Berry Head is a coastal headland that forms the southern boundary of Tor Bay in Devon, England [1]. Lying to the east of the town of Brixham, it is a national nature reserve and a local nature reserve [1]. Berry Head is the site of an Iron Age hill fort which was mostly destroyed by the construction between 1794 and 1804 of extensive fortifications to protect the Torbay naval anchorage against threatened inva