]. Based on radiocarbon dating of coals discovered underneath the base, the menhir is believed to have been raised around 5000 BCE, in the Neo-Chalcolithic period, approximately the same time as the Coureleiros dolmens, or megalithic tombs, that are found in the same district [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:149547", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-011: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/521ade1a/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/521ade1a/MenhirofMeada.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
