etres at the base [1]. It weighs around 18 tons [1]. Based on radiocarbon dating of coals discovered underneath the base, the menhir is believed to have been raised around 5000 BCE, in the Neo-Chalcolithic period, approximately the same time as the Coureleiros dolmens, or megalithic tombs, that are found in the same district [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:149547", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-011: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/521ade1a/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/521ade1a/MenhirofMeada.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('5290a257-c16d-444a-8620-aa60ec6130da'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '2', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:5290a257-c16d-444a-8620-aa60ec6130da:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''2'' restored on Albanopolis', '5b552072008d56562b684b6a1b25881c', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''Undated'') is shared by 120 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:43507", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0074:chunk-0001: description ''Albanopolis was an ancient Illyrian settlement identified with the archaeological site of Zgerdhesh, southwest of Kruje in central Albania. Founded in the 4th century BC, it reached its peak in the 3rd century BC before being abandoned after the Roman conquest in the 2nd century BC. Powerful walls stretching 1,400 metres enclosed the town, with an acropolis occupying nearly a third of the site. The geographer Ptolemy recorded the Albanoi tribe here around AD 150, possibly linking it to the origin of the name Albania.'' -> ''Albanopolis was a city of the Albanoi, an Illyrian tribe [1]. The city appears in the literature in 150 AD, almost 300 years after Roman conquest of the region [1]. The toponym Albanopolis has been found on a funeral inscription in Gorno Sonje, near the city of Skopje, present-day North Macedonia [1]. It was discovered in 1931 by Nikola Vulić and its text was analyzed and published in 1982 by Borka Dragojević-Josifovska [1]. Ptolemy (100-170 AD) is the only author who mentions Albanopolis [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_l