09:chunk-0001: description \"The Lia Fáil (Stone of Destiny) is a megalithic stone on the Hill of Tara''s Inauguration Mound in County Meath, Ireland, used as the coronation seat for the King of Tara and High King of Ireland [1]. Legend claims all Irish kings were crowned on this stone until Muirchertach mac Ercae c. 500 AD [1]. The stone was believed to possess magical properties, notably ''screaming'' when a rightful king stood upon it [1].\" -> \"The Lia Fáil (Stone of Destiny) is a megalithic stone on the Hill of Tara''s Inauguration Mound in County Meath, Ireland [1] [2] [3]. Legend claims all Irish kings were crowned on this stone until Muirchertach mac Ercae c. 500 AD [1]. The stone was believed to possess magical properties [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348255", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348256", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
