emediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4309:chunk-0001: description \"The Lia Fáil (Stone of Destiny) is a megalithic stone on the Hill of Tara''s Inauguration Mound in County Meath, Ireland, used as the coronation seat for the King of Tara and High King of Ireland [1]. Legend claims all Irish kings were crowned on this stone until Muirchertach mac Ercae c. 500 AD [1]. The stone was believed to possess magical properties, notably ''screaming'' when a rightful king stood upon it [1].\" -> \"The Lia Fáil (Stone of Destiny) is a megalithic stone on the Hill of Tara''s Inauguration Mound in County Meath, Ireland [1] [2] [3]. Legend claims all Irish kings were crowned on this stone until Muirchertach mac Ercae c. 500 AD [1]. The stone was believed to possess magical properties [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348255", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348256", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('52fe4aef-2fab-4d5b-9a5c-19b7f491a7fb'::uuid, 'antiquity', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:52fe4aef-2fab-4d5b-9a5c-19b7f491a7fb:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: antiquity ''5'' restored on El Castillón', '8702b93be1d0f443f9886db0dbf26d5d', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 6 from period_start -1500"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:43509", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0074:chunk-0001: description ''El Castillon is a fortified Late Roman settlement in Santa Eulalia de Tabara, Zamora, Spain, situated on the historical frontier between the Swabian and Visigothic kingdoms. Occupied from the Iron Age, its peak period spans the 5th to 8th centuries AD, making it crucial for understanding the transition from Late Antiquity to the Early Middle Ages. Excavations since 2007 have uncovered a structured urban plan with specialized metalworking districts for iron production, thick enclosing walls, and over 6,000 pottery fragments. The site controlled the Esla River valley and nearby iron ore mines.'' -> ''El Castillón is an archaeological site located in the Spanish hamlet of Santa Eulalia de Tábara, in the municipality of Moreruela de Tábara, province of Zamora [1]. The site covers an area of about 4 hectares and is situated over a plateau at the top of a hill located on the right riverside of the River Esla [1]. The site has been inhabited since the Iron Age, but the most known period of the site belongs to the Late Roman Era as a large number of late Hispano-Roman red gloss pottery testifies [1]. Excavations have been carried out since 2007 to date with a gap year in 2015 [1]. In a shelter located just few meters below the site, some samples of schematic art have been discovered [1]. The images represent human-like icons, sticks, fingers, anchor-shaped symbols, circles and indefinites [1]. Painted in red colour on quartzite, they belong to the Bronze Age with an age of more than 3000 years [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98898", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s008: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:98899", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s008: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:149562", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-011: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/52fe4aef/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/52fe4aef/Excavación_en_el_Castillón_(2013).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237615", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237616", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''401''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:311125", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-006: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/52fe4aef/Excavación_en_el_Castillón_(2013).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/52fe4aef/Cerámica_gris_estampillada.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348257", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348258", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s003: period_start ''401'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:400329", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''Undated'' -> '