t Buryan in Cornwall, considered one of the best-preserved fogous in the county. Unusual for having more than one entrance, it features a main passage with classic dry-stone and lintel construction plus a side chamber. Excavation yielded Iron Age pottery and a carved figure with a raised arm holding an unidentified object, possibly a spear. A 1996 Time Team investigation discovered remains of an early Iron Age house enclosed by an oval wall adjacent to the fogou, suggesting ritual or ceremonial use.'' -> ''Boleigh Fogou is an Iron Age underground dry-stone passage near St Buryan in Cornwall, considered one of the best-preserved fogous in the county [1] [2] [3]. Unusual for having more than one entrance, it features a main passage with classic dry-stone and lintel construction [1] [2]. Excavation yielded Iron Age pottery [1] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348996", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:348997", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:400331", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:400332", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start None -> ''-1500''"}]'::jsonb),
