rton Bavant in Wiltshire, England. The fort covers 15 hectares (37 acres) and occupies the summit of the hill on the edge of Salisbury Plain. Its four-sided earthworks follow the natural contours of the hilltop, enclosing one of the larger hillforts in Wiltshire.[1]'' -> ''Scratchbury Camp is an Iron Age univallate hillfort on Scratchbury Hill, overlooking the Wylye valley about 1 km northeast of Norton Bavant in Wiltshire, England [1]. The fort occupies the summit of the hill on the edge of Salisbury Plain [1]. Its four-sided earthworks follow the natural contours of the hilltop [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345680", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:345681", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-09a_fields-wd5-s001: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:400333", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:400334", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start None -> ''-1500''"}]'::jsonb),
