, which is a Scheduled Ancient Monument [1]. In archaeological circles, the hill fort is known as Cadbury-Congresbury in order to differentiate it from the Cadbury Castle hillfort in South Cadbury [1]. It appears to have been constructed in the Iron Age when one or more ramparts, with walls and ditches, were built on the steep slopes of the hill to defend an area covering some eight and a half acres [1]. The remains of Iron Age round houses may still be seen inside [1]. The hill fort was refortified around 400, after the urban collapse associated with the withdrawal of Rome, and occupation extended into the sub-Roman period [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117601", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117602", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117603", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: site_type ''Fortress/citadel'' -> ''Fort''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150194", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-012: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/574b24e0/hero.webp'' -> ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/56/ST4464_Ancient_Hill_Fort%2C_Cadbury_Hill_-_geograph.org.uk_-_68763.jpg''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248723", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s008: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248724", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s008: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:333832", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-001: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/56/ST4464_Ancient_Hill_Fort%2C_Cadbury_Hill_-_geograph.org.uk_-_68763.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wik