tanding Stone. Despite its significance, the cromlech remains unscheduled and lacks formal heritage protection.\" -> \"Tregele is a small village in northern Anglesey, Wales, near which stands the Llanfechell Cromlech [1]. Late Neolithic and Early Bronze Age rock art was discovered on one of the monument''s stones in 2004-2005 by Dr. George Nash [2] [3]. The site sits within a distinctive prehistoric burial-ritual landscape alongside the Meini Hirion stone group and the Llanfechell Standing Stone [2] [3]. The cromlech remains unscheduled and lacks formal heritage protection [2].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349039", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349040", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('5a5beef1-9bd1-472e-b77d-eefe6092cb06'::uuid, 'antiquity', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:5a5beef1-9bd1-472e-b77d-eefe6092cb06:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: antiquity ''5'' restored on Slwch Tump', '67e9c139ab37d01c2df54d6e5052479f', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 6 from period_start -1500"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:84704", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2094:chunk-0001: description ''Slwch Tump, also known as Slwch Camp, is an Iron Age hillfort on a sandstone hill at 246 m elevation, about 1.3 km east of Brecon in Powys, Wales. The roughly rectangular enclosure measures approximately 187 by 242 metres with a single encircling scarp 3-4.6 m high and no ditch. Its entrance faces northwest toward Brecon. The hillfort lies within territory attributed to the Silures, a pre-Roman tribe of southeast Wales, and clusters with nearby forts at Pen-y-crug and Coed Fenni-fach, suggesting substantial late prehistoric population in the area.'' -> ''Slwch Tump, also known as Slwch Camp and formerly known as Pen Cevn-y-Gaer, is an Iron Age hillfort close to Brecon in Powys [1]. The enclosure is located on a hill composed of sandstones of the St Maughans Formation with an elevation of 807 ft, about 0.8 miles east of the confluence of the Rivers Usk and Honddu in the centre of Brecon [1]. The hillfort is smaller than the one on nearby Pen-y-crug and is irregular but roughly rectangular in shape, measuring about 187 m by 242 m [1]. Within the hillfort area there are remains of abandoned quarries for building stone [1]. A small church stood for some time at Slwch Tump, marking the place where Saint Eluned was supposedly beheaded [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:99936", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:99937", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150332", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-012: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Slwch_Tump_-_geograph.org.uk_-_344523.jpg/400px-Slwch_Tump_-_geograph.org.uk_-_344523.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5a5beef1/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248759", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s008: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248760", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s008: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385784", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385785", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:400345", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:400346", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start None -> ''-1500''"}]'::jsonb),
