st entrances [1]. Evidence was also discovered for several enclosures or buildings inside the fort [1]. Arbury Banks has been suggested as a possible location for the Battle of Watling Street, where a small Roman force destroyed the army of Boudica [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:99968", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:99969", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''-2000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237695", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:237696", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s004: period_start None -> ''-1000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:333853", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-001: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5bac3b4e/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5bac3b4e/Arbury_banks.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('5c3a138c-7052-4cb4-a482-10df27239b2e'::uuid, 'mystery', '1', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:5c3a138c-7052-4cb4-a482-10df27239b2e:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''4'' restored on Padderbury Top', 'b8106db440c25934ffe73eb997311b3e', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 1 from (''Fortress/citadel'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 235 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:27830", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0015:chunk-0001: site_type ''City/town/settlement'' -> ''Fortress/citadel''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:34585", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0032:chunk-0001: description ''Padderbury Top is an Iron Age defended settlement (hillfort) about 3.2 km south-east of Menheniot in Cornwall, England. The roughly circular enclosure has an interior diameter of approximately 73 metres, with an inner rampart 9 metres wide and 3 metres high. Aerial photographs reveal originally up to four lines of defence with associated ditches, now largely preserved as buried features. The monument is scheduled under the Ancient Monuments and Archaeological Areas Act 1979 as being of national importance, occupying a prominent skyline position with commanding views across the surrounding landscape.'' -> ''Padderbury Top is a hillfort about 2 miles (3.2 km) south-east of Menheniot, in Cornwall, England, named after the hill on which it is situated [1]. It is a scheduled monument [1]. The enclosure is roughly circular [1]. The diameter of the interior, which has been ploughed, is about 80 yards (73 m) [1]. There is one surviving rampart, 2–3 feet (0.61–0.91 m) above the interior, and 10 feet (3.0 m) externally [1]. There are entrances on the west and east sides [1]. The rampart is surrounded by a belt of flat ground about 60 feet (18 m) wide and about 3 feet (0.91 m) high: aerial photographs show that this area was originally outer defences, since reduced by ploughing [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:99979", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:99980", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''-2000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150910", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-013: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f1/Padderbury_Top_-_geograph.org.uk_-_171437.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5c3a138c/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248785", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s008: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248786", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s008: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349060", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349061", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:354777", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-19r_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:354778", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-19r_fields-wd5-s001: period_start None -> ''-800''"}]'::jsonb),
