ssic Period [1]. In the late 8th century AD through to the early 9th century, Sacul was one of the few kingdoms in the southeastern Petén region to use its own Emblem Glyph, together with Ixtutz and Ucanal [1]. In AD 779 Sacul went to war against Ixkun and lost, but stelae at both cities record a visit to Ixkun by king Ch''iyel of Sacul just 11 years later and the two cities appear to have formed a military alliance at that time [1]. The site core is arranged around a number of plazas, one of which forms a monumental acropolis [1]. The site core includes pyramids, a ballcourt, a triadic complex and two E-Group astronomical complexes [1]. The last stela erected in Sacul bears a date corresponding to AD 800 [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100023", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_name ''500 - 1000 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100024", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s009: period_start ''500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:150984", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-013: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Sacul_emblem_glyph.gif/400px-Sacul_emblem_glyph.gif'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/5df03f8d/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248807", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s008: period_name None -> ''500 - 1000 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248808", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s008: period_start None -> ''500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349076", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''500 - 1000 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349077", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:400353", "url": "remediation_