from what is now Hamble Point [1]. The site is now referred to as Hamble Common Camp [1]. This is believed to be an Iron Age settlement, with the ditch being a defensive structure [1]. The ''wet nature'' of the area has ensured that most of these structures have remained intact [1]. Some have suggested this site could have been a promontory fort [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35786", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: site_type ''Settlement'' -> ''Fortress/citadel''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117707", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117708", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117709", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: site_type ''Fortress/citadel'' -> ''Fort''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:117710", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s004: source_url ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamble_Common_Camp'' -> ''https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamble_Common''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151012", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/5e710f8a/hero.webp'' -> ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/81/Earthwork_on_Hamble_Common_-_geograph.org.uk_-_295021.jpg''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248813", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s008: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:248814", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s008: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:333871", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-001: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/