_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4317:chunk-0001: description ''A large basaltic rock carving at the archaeological complex of Zonzamas on Lanzarote, Canary Islands, interpreted as a prehistoric lunisolar calendar with 12 solar and 13 lunar months, similar in structure to the ancient Egyptian calendar. Six carved channels represent the first six Canarian months of the Atxano year, which began at the summer solstice. The site is associated with the aboriginal Guanche/Majo culture and is argued to predate Punic or Roman contact, pointing to an Atlantic Bronze Age megalithic cultural horizon. Cart-ruts and Iberian-Guanche rock inscriptions found nearby further suggest a complex pre-classical prehistory for the islands.'' -> ''A large basaltic rock carving at the archaeological complex of Zonzamas on Lanzarote, Canary Islands, interpreted as a prehistoric lunisolar calendar with 12 solar and 13 lunar months, similar in structure to the ancient Egyptian calendar [1] [2]. The site is associated with the aboriginal Guanche/Majo culture and is argued to predate Punic or Roman contact, pointing to an Atlantic Bronze Age megalithic cultural horizon [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349125", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349126", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''-10000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('669d6f3d-fb65-47ce-907a-3b6c847666d4'::uuid, 'mystery', '4', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:669d6f3d-fb65-47ce-907a-3b6c847666d4:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''5'' restored on Temple of Kom Ombo', '75ebd074183ea99b878f3dc361c6a079', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 4 from (''Temple complex'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 53 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:85048", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2103:chunk-0001: description ''A unique double temple on the Nile at Kom Ombo in Upper Egypt, begun by Ptolemy VI Philometor (180-145 BC) and expanded by subsequent Ptolemaic rulers and Romans. Its unprecedented dual design features symmetrically duplicated courts, halls, and sanctuaries dedicated to two deities: the crocodile god Sobek in the southern half and the falcon god Haroeris (Horus the Elder) in the northern half. The inner rear wall bears a notable relief believed to depict ancient surgical instruments. Much of the temple has been damaged by Nile flooding, earthquakes, and stone quarrying over the centuries.'' -> ''The Temple of Kom Ombo is an unusual double temple in the town of Kom Ombo in Aswan Governorate, Upper Egypt [1]. It was constructed during the Ptolemaic dynasty, 180–47 BC [1]. Some additions to it were later made during the Roman period [1]. The building is unique because its \\''double\\'' design meant that there were courts, halls, sanctuaries and rooms duplicated for two sets of gods [1]. The southern half of the temple was dedicated to the crocodile god Sobek [1]. The northern part of the temple was dedicated to the falcon god Haroeris (\"Horus the Elder\") [1]. A temple was already built in the New Kingdom to honor these gods, however, this site gained in importance during the Ptolemaic Kingdom [1]. Some of the reliefs inside were defaced by Copts, who once used the temple as a church [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151739", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-014: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bc/Kom_Ombo_Portal_04.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/669d6f3d/Ptolemy_VI_relief,_Temple_of_Kom_Ombo,_Egypt_-_20070306.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312084", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/669d6f3d/Ptolemy_VI_relief,_Temple_of_Kom_Ombo,_Egypt_-_20070306.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/669d6f3d/Kom_Ombo_Portal_04.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
