]. The northern part of the temple was dedicated to the falcon god Haroeris (\"Horus the Elder\") [1]. A temple was already built in the New Kingdom to honor these gods, however, this site gained in importance during the Ptolemaic Kingdom [1]. Some of the reliefs inside were defaced by Copts, who once used the temple as a church [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:151739", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-014: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bc/Kom_Ombo_Portal_04.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/669d6f3d/Ptolemy_VI_relief,_Temple_of_Kom_Ombo,_Egypt_-_20070306.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312084", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/669d6f3d/Ptolemy_VI_relief,_Temple_of_Kom_Ombo,_Egypt_-_20070306.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/669d6f3d/Kom_Ombo_Portal_04.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
