    ('67b3a2f7-5f1b-46cc-893a-6cc48b2908c4'::uuid, 'antiquity', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:67b3a2f7-5f1b-46cc-893a-6cc48b2908c4:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: antiquity ''5'' restored on Wapley Hill', '0f6c430ede620011f44f0ab58d846ada', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 6 from period_start -1500"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:34835", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0034:chunk-0001: description ''Wapley Hill is a large multivallate Iron Age hillfort in Herefordshire, 3 km southeast of Presteigne, occupying approximately 5.5 hectares on a west-facing escarpment. The roughly triangular fort features massive southern defences with five ramparts and ditches, and a complex inturned entrance passage. A late Bronze Age ritual shaft sunk to 33 m depth suggests the site may have served as a Celtic religious centre rather than purely defensive. Four unexcavated pillow mounds within the enclosure further support its possible sacred function. The site is a Scheduled Monument.'' -> \"Wapley Hill is an Iron Age hill fort in Herefordshire, England, 3 km south-east of Presteigne [1]. Wapley Hill stands in mixed woodland on a west-facing escarpment to the south of the B4362 road from Presteigne to Mortimer''s Cross [1]. The defences stand at a height of 5.6 m and occupy 6 hectares [1]. The entrance is situated on the southern side and comprises a 90 m passage [1]. A ''ritual shaft'' dating from the late Bronze Age is sunk to a depth of 33 m [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100857", "url": "re