 down the southeast side [1]. The northeast stone is 4.2 metres high and is of rectangular section—the stone leans to the northwest [1]. The stones were first recorded by William Borlase in 1754 [1]. His descendant William Copeland Borlase excavated the stones in 1871 with no result [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100915", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:100916", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:152270", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-015: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3a/%22The_Pipers%22_standing_stones_near_Boleigh_Farm_-_geograph.org.uk_-_41054.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/6b6a62fc/The Pipers 05.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249287", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:249288", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s009: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349157", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349158", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s004: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385842", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385843", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''-2500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
