2] [4]. One of only about 150 such hillforts in England, it may have served as a stock enclosure, redistribution centre, or settlement [2] [3]. The wider site is a National Nature Reserve, SSSI, and Special Area of Conservation renowned for its ancient pollarded beech trees [1] [5] [6].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385852", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385853", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
