url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4321:chunk-0001: description ''The Cave of Bacinete (Cueva de Bacinete) is located in Los Alcornocales Natural Park near Los Barrios in Andalusia, southern Spain. It contains prehistoric rock art depicting animals, people, and symbols created using natural pigments. The art spans multiple periods: semi-schematic paintings in dark red from the early Neolithic, and white schematic paintings from the late Neolithic to Metal Age. Declared a Property of Cultural Interest in 1985, it is one of only eight rock shelters in southern Spain physically protected for its rock art.'' -> ''The Cave of Bacinete (Cueva de Bacinete) is located in Los Alcornocales Natural Park near Los Barrios in Andalusia, southern Spain [1]. It contains prehistoric rock art depicting animals, people, and symbols created using natural pigments [1] [2] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349923", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349924", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_start ''-10000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('7149fb1e-d88f-459a-88e1-c5547c8b1138'::uuid, 'mystery', '4', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:7149fb1e-d88f-459a-88e1-c5547c8b1138:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''5'' restored on San Gervasio', '415ec527c0b49efdaf7ca00fd080c594', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 4 from (''Temple complex'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 53 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:80982", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2015:chunk-0001: description \"San Gervasio is the most important Maya archaeological site on Cozumel Island, located in the Mexican state of Quintana Roo. It served as a major pilgrimage sanctuary dedicated to the goddess Ix Chel, deity of childbirth, fertility, and medicine, attracting Maya women from across Mesoamerica. The site reached peak prominence during the Post-Classic period (1200-1530 CE), with nine temple buildings arranged around an enclosed central courtyard connected by three sacbe roads. Its pre-Hispanic name was Tantun Cuzamil, meaning ''Flat Rock in the Place of the Swallows''. Juan de Grijalva was the first European to visit in 1518, followed by Hernan Cortes in 1519.\" -> \"San Gervasio is an archaeological site of the pre-Columbian Maya civilization, located in the northern third of the island of Cozumel off the northeastern coast of the Yucatán Peninsula, in what is now the Mexican state of Quintana Roo [1]. San Gervasio''s pre-Hispanic name was Tantun Cuzamil, Mayan for Flat Rock in the place of the Swallows [1]. The ruins were once a hub of worship of the goddess Ix Chel, an aged deity of childbirth, fertility, medicine, and weaving [1]. San Gervasio was founded around 300 CE as a small community [1]. Around 600, it began a period of rapid growth, with new construction and possible stronger connections with settlements on the northern coast of Quintana Roo [1]. After about 1000, San Gervasio expanded significantly, possibly influenced by the growing political and economic importance of Chichén Itzá [1]. By about 1200, San Gervasio had become the largest settlement on Cozumel and remained so until the arrival of the Spanish in the early 16th century [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101023", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''1000 - 1500 AD'' -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101024", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''1000'' -> ''-200''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:152437", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-015: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c1/Los_Murcielagos%2C_San_Gervasio.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/7149fb1e/Altar,_San_Gervasio.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312280", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/7149fb1e/Altar,_San_Gervasio.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/7149fb1e/Los_Murcielagos,_San_Gervasio.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
