 an aged deity of childbirth, fertility, medicine, and weaving [1]. San Gervasio was founded around 300 CE as a small community [1]. Around 600, it began a period of rapid growth, with new construction and possible stronger connections with settlements on the northern coast of Quintana Roo [1]. After about 1000, San Gervasio expanded significantly, possibly influenced by the growing political and economic importance of Chichén Itzá [1]. By about 1200, San Gervasio had become the largest settlement on Cozumel and remained so until the arrival of the Spanish in the early 16th century [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101023", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''1000 - 1500 AD'' -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101024", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''1000'' -> ''-200''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:152437", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-015: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c1/Los_Murcielagos%2C_San_Gervasio.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/7149fb1e/Altar,_San_Gervasio.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312280", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/7149fb1e/Altar,_San_Gervasio.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/7149fb1e/Los_Murcielagos,_San_Gervasio.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
