were once a hub of worship of the goddess Ix Chel, an aged deity of childbirth, fertility, medicine, and weaving [1]. San Gervasio was founded around 300 CE as a small community [1]. Around 600, it began a period of rapid growth, with new construction and possible stronger connections with settlements on the northern coast of Quintana Roo [1]. After about 1000, San Gervasio expanded significantly, possibly influenced by the growing political and economic importance of Chichén Itzá [1]. By about 1200, San Gervasio had become the largest settlement on Cozumel and remained so until the arrival of the Spanish in the early 16th century [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101023", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_name ''1000 - 1500 AD'' -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101024", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s010: period_start ''1000'' -> ''-200''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:152437", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-015: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c1/Los_Murcielagos%2C_San_Gervasio.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/7149fb1e/Altar,_San_Gervasio.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312280", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-007: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/7149fb1e/Altar,_San_Gervasio.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/7149fb1e/Los_Murcielagos,_San_Gervasio.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('7155aa5a-4eff-4b1d-a105-b15d17b786c6'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:7155aa5a-4eff-4b1d-a105-b15d17b786c6:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''4'' restored on Kirkdale Cave', 'd6b32a19c40df20e2c7ed7380ed49bca', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Cave Structures'', ''Undated'') is shared by 33 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:44511", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0096:chunk-0001: description ''Kirkdale Cave is a fossil site near Kirkbymoorside in the Vale of Pickering, North Yorkshire, England. Discovered by quarry workers in 1821, it contained fossilised bones of hippos, elephants, cave hyenas, cave lions, and rhinoceroses dating to the Eemian interglacial around 121,000 years ago. It is one of the northernmost sites where hippopotamus remains have been found. William Buckland analysed the cave in December 1821, determining the bones were brought by hyenas who used it as a den, and was awarded the Copley Medal in 1822 for his landmark paper.'' -> ''Kirkdale Cave is a cave and fossil site located in Kirkdale near Kirkbymoorside in the Vale of Pickering, North Yorkshire, England [1]. William Buckland analyzed the cave and its contents in December 1821 and determined that the bones were the remains of animals brought in by hyenas who used it for a den, and not a result of the Biblical flood floating corpses in from distant lands, as he had first thought [1]. The fossil bones found in the cave included those of straight-tusked elephants, hippopotamuses, the narrow-nosed rhinoceros, cave hyena, cave lion, Irish elk, brown bears, red deer and fallow deer [1]. The fossilized remains were embedded in a silty layer sandwiched between layers of stalagmite [1]. The entrance to the cave was found by limestone quarry workers in the summer of 1821 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101665", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_name ''< 4500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101666", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_start ''-121000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:152438", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/7155aa5a/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/7155aa5a/Kirkdale Cave - geograph.org.uk - 1072214.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:304103", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04e_period-label-undated: period_name None -> ''Undated''"}]'::jsonb),
