 farmstead are also present. A Late Medieval cowhouse was built inside the walls of one courtyard house. The settlement is a Scheduled Monument and provides key evidence for the distinctive Iron Age habitation pattern of southwest England.\" -> \"Bosporthennis is a Late Iron Age settlement in the civil parish of Zennor on the Penwith peninsula, west Cornwall, England [1]. The site comprises at least three courtyard houses at the eastern foot of Hannibal''s Carn [1]. An adjoining field system and a medieval farmstead are also present [2] [3]. A Late Medieval cowhouse was built inside the walls of one courtyard house [1]. The settlement is a Scheduled Monument [2] [3].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349949", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349950", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
