ns'' to Wheeler''s excavation report.\" -> ''Lydney Park in Gloucestershire contains a late Roman temple complex atop an Iron Age hillfort [1]. The rectangular temple was dedicated to Nodens, a Celtic healing and hunting deity linked to the Welsh Lludd and Irish Nuada [2] [3] [4]. The complex included a bath suite with hypocaust heating and a large guest house for pilgrims [1] [2] [5].''"}]'::jsonb),
