nge_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4324:chunk-0001: description ''Sturminster Newton Castle is an Iron Age promontory fort reused as a medieval manorial site, located on a triangular limestone spur above the River Stour in Dorset, England. The crescent-shaped defences feature a bank 40 feet wide and 6-10 feet high with a ditch 50-60 feet wide and up to 20 feet deep, enclosing approximately 4 acres. Within the prehistoric earthworks stands a 14th-century manor house built for Glastonbury Abbey, surviving as a two-storey roofless ruin of rubble and ashlar. The site is privately owned and not accessible to visitors.'' -> ''Sturminster Newton Castle is an Iron Age promontory fort reused as a medieval manorial site, located on a triangular limestone spur above the River Stour in Dorset, England [1] [2]. The crescent-shaped defences feature a bank 40 feet wide and 6-10 feet high with a ditch 50-60 feet wide and up to 20 feet deep [2]. Within the prehistoric earthworks stands a 14th-century manor house built for Glastonbury Abbey, surviving as a roofless ruin of rubble and ashlar [1]. The site is privately owned and not accessible to visitors [1] [3].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385876", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385877", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:400427", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:400428", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start None -> ''-1500''"}]'::jsonb),
