"source": "remediation_change_log:338397", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4wc:p4wc-4324:chunk-0001: description ''Colebrooke is a village and parish in Devon, England, about 5 miles (8 km) west of Crediton[1]. The site is notable for remains of a Roman road agger visible in a field roughly 300 metres south of Rag Lane, east of Five Acre Copse[2]. This road maintained its route from North Tawton, becoming less distinct at Colebrooke, though a straight lane along the ridge east of the railway suggests its original line[2]. Colebrooke is believed to be the location of a Roman settlement, though documentation is fragmentary[3].'' -> ''Colebrooke is a village and parish in Devon, England, about 5 miles (8 km) west of Crediton [1]. Remains of a Roman road agger visible in a field roughly 300 metres south of Rag Lane, east of Five Acre Copse [1] [2]. This road maintained its route from North Tawton, becoming less distinct at Colebrooke, though a straight lane along the ridge east of the railway suggests its original line [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349968", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:349969", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_start ''1'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
