nown in Portugal. The menhirs have a star-like appearance with an ellipsoidal cross-section and are engraved with circles and dimples. Discovered in 1992, a recovery project later restored and re-erected the stones in their original cavities.'' -> ''A group of menhirs in the parish of Alcoutim e Pereiro, Algarve, Portugal, likely erected during the second half of the 4th millennium BC [1] [2]. The largest stands over 3 metres tall and is carved from greywacke, a dark grey stone with a brown patinated surface, making it the largest example of greywacke menhirs known in Portugal [1] [2] [3]. The menhirs have an ellipsoidal cross-section and are engraved with circles and dimples [2] [4].''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('77eab45e-3a34-4ebd-abb0-ac6431b72b42'::uuid, 'antiquity', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:77eab45e-3a34-4ebd-abb0-ac6431b72b42:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: antiquity ''5'' restored on Castle Rings, Wiltshire', '7a298bc32fa1ed11bced2dc598e7470c', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 6 from period_start -1500"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:85456", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2114:chunk-0001: description ''Castle Rings is a univallate hill fort in Donhead St Mary parish, Wiltshire, dating to the Iron Age (c. 800 BC - 1st century AD). The site sits at 228 metres (748 ft) elevation on Upper Greensand sandstone and is a Scheduled Ancient Monument. While most of the fortification lies within Donhead St Mary, some outlying earthworks extend into the neighbouring parish of Sedgehill and Semley. In the mid-1980s, a metal detectorist discovered a hoard of stater coins within the hill fort.[1]'' -> ''Castle Rings is a univallate hill fort in the parish of Donhead St Mary in Wiltshire [1]. Castle Rings has been dated to the Iron Age and is at an altitude of 228 metres upon Upper Greensand sandstone beds [1]. In the mid-1980s a metal detectorist unearthed a hoard of stater coins of the Durotriges tribe within the hill fort [1]. The fort measures 320 by 200 metres, enclosing an area of 5.2 hectares [1]. There is a counter-scarp bank that averages 5 metres wide and varies in height from 3.1 metres at the southwest to between 0.8 and 1.5 metres at the northeast; at the southwest this bank is high enough to give the impression of a bivallate fort [1]. There are four gaps in the ramparts, one in each of the cardinal directions, but it is not known if these were original entrances to the fort [1]. The coins, which are attributed to the Durotriges, are now in the collection of the British Museum [1]. They were dug up on 13 October 1985 with twelve ceramic fragments; 88 coins were found in all, some 30 of these were said to be contained within the broken pottery [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101791", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101792", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:153146", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-016: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/77eab45e/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/77eab45e/Castle Rings, Donhead St Mary 01.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250121", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250122", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312994", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-008: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/77eab45e/Castle Rings, Donhead St Mary 01.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/77eab45e/Entrance to Castle Rings Fort - geograph.org.uk - 427428.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385886", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385887", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_