es at the northeast; at the southwest this bank is high enough to give the impression of a bivallate fort [1]. There are four gaps in the ramparts, one in each of the cardinal directions, but it is not known if these were original entrances to the fort [1]. The coins, which are attributed to the Durotriges, are now in the collection of the British Museum [1]. They were dug up on 13 October 1985 with twelve ceramic fragments; 88 coins were found in all, some 30 of these were said to be contained within the broken pottery [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101791", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:101792", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s011: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:153146", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-016: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/77eab45e/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/77eab45e/Castle Rings, Donhead St Mary 01.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250121", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250122", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:312994", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-008: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/77eab45e/Castle Rings, Donhead St Mary 01.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/77eab45e/Entrance to Castle Rings Fort - geograph.org.uk - 427428.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385886", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:385887", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period