e of the hill for the purpose of enclosing this spring [1]. This rampart appears to have had only two entrances, one on the north and the other on the south side; just within the entrenchment, at the entrance on the north, is a small tumulus, which may have been constructed as a mount for observation or defense, or for the purpose of interment [1]. The name shows that the later Saxon settlers in the region found the earthworks so impressive that they thought they must have been built by the chief of their gods, Woden alias Grim [1]. The site lies at an elevation of 155m AOD [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:102582", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s012: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:102583", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s012: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250203", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250204", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s011: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:313158", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-008: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/80ea9e97/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/80ea9e97/Grimsbury Castle, Iron Age Hill Fort - geograph.org.uk - 886.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386515", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386516", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:400481", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s002: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "r