pear as a considerable municipal community [1]. Its name is also found both in Pliny, who reckons it among the populi stipendiarii of the island, and in Ptolemy [1]. We find no later notice of it, though an inscription of Christian times found at Catana appears to refer to Hybla as still existing under its ancient name [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:102668", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s012: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:102669", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s012: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250599", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s012: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250600", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s012: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350051", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350052", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s005: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
