 681 BC [1]. As with the reliefs at Khinnis, the reliefs at Halamata Cave are \"associated with the northern canal system built by the Assyrian king Sennacherib (r. 704-681 BCE) to carry water to his capital city of Nineveh\" [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:154608", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-018: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/84894867/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/84894867/Maltai_Reliefs_-_Halamata_Cave.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
