    ('8793ca33-397e-47a5-a6bb-020802f49e7c'::uuid, 'antiquity', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:8793ca33-397e-47a5-a6bb-020802f49e7c:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: antiquity ''5'' restored on Garn Boduan', '2394465e01b3f4b43df2446cbb2269a8', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 6 from period_start -1500"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81062", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2018:chunk-0001: description ''Iron Age hillfort on the Llyn Peninsula near Nefyn, Wales, enclosing approximately 10 hectares at 250m elevation. Surveys documented about 170 stone-walled round house foundations, suggesting a community of 100-400 people. The lower stone rampart is the original Iron Age defence, while a fortified citadel (60x30m) on the eastern side was likely added during the early medieval period, possibly serving as a castle of Welsh princes. Finds include a stone axe head, slingstones, and Roman glass beads.'' -> ''Garn Boduan is an Iron Age hillfort and hill near Nefyn, on the Llŷn Peninsula in Wales [1]. In a survey in the 1950s the traces of over 170 round houses were identified on this site, and around 100 round houses are still visible on the ground [1]. Between 100 and 400 people may have lived in this fort [1]. The lower stone rampart is the original defence built in the Iron Age [1]. At a later date, perhaps in the 6th/7th century AD, a smaller rampart was built on the eastern side [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103345", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1