    ('8c8043b6-5c87-4366-9f84-acf61dee4294'::uuid, 'antiquity', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:8c8043b6-5c87-4366-9f84-acf61dee4294:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: antiquity ''5'' restored on Castle Knowe, Northumberland', 'cf826195e01aa81aa821e3512da7156e', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 6 from period_start -1500"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:85904", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2127:chunk-0001: description ''Castle Knowe, also known as Clinch Castle, is a multivallate Iron Age hillfort in the Cheviot Hills of Northumberland, about 1.6 km south-east of Ingram. The fort summit measures approximately 75 metres by 60 metres, defended by three roughly concentric ramparts formed by scarping the natural slope, standing up to 2.8 metres externally. The outer and middle ramparts merge on the steep western side. An original entrance on the east side features slightly inturned rampart ends. Remains of seven or more roundhouses survive within the enclosure. The fort is part of a dense concentration of Iron Age settlement in the Breamish Valley, with contemporary hillforts visible on Old Fawden Hill and Chubden Hill. It is a scheduled monument.'' -> \"Castle Knowe, also known as Clinch Castle, is the site of an Iron Age hillfort in Northumberland, England, about 1 mile south-east of the village of Ingram [1]. It is a scheduled monument [1]. The fort is in the Cheviot Hills, where there are other Iron Age sites including those at Old Fawden Hill and Chubden Hill, visible from Castle Knowe to the south-west [1]. The hill has steep slopes to the west and north, less steep to the east and south [1]. The fort on the summit measures about 75 metres west to east and 60 metres north to south; there are three roughly concentric ramparts on the slopes of the hill, of which the outer rampart and middle ramparts merge on the west side [1]. The fort''s outer rampart is the most substantial [1]. There is an original entrance on the east side, where the rampart''s ends are slightly inturned [1]. There are remains of seven or more roundhouses within the fort, of diameter 3.8 to 8.4 metres; there is some overlapping, indicating that there was more than one phase of occupation [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103413", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103414", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s013: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250677", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s012: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:250678", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s012: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386553", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386554", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:401117", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:401118", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_start None -> ''-1500''"}]'::jsonb),
