    ('8d5b27e6-c0ab-4c08-8742-7bb0c59bcfa5'::uuid, 'mystery', '7', '8', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:8d5b27e6-c0ab-4c08-8742-7bb0c59bcfa5:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''8'' restored on Villa of Torre de Palma', 'adc03e67b4fd8b7e6f0a6d1e5dd52ddd', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 7 from (''Residence/villa/farmhouse'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 6 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:85916", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2127:chunk-0001: description ''The Villa Lusitano-Romana de Torre de Palma is a Roman villa near Monforte in Portugal, in the Roman province of Lusitania[1]. It is considered one of the largest villas in the Iberian Peninsula[1]. The estate prospered through latifundia agriculture, evidenced by shrines found in its courtyard[1]. The complex includes extensive living areas, a basilica, and a remarkable seven-roomed baptistery[1].'' -> ''The villa of Torre de Palma is located about 5 km northwest of Monforte on the main road to Vaiamonte  [1]. The remains of the villa were discovered in 1947 and until 1956, excavations were conducted under the direction of the Portuguese archaeologist Manuel Heleno [1]. The chronology of the various periods of the villa ranges from the 1st to the 5th century [1]. In addition to a large residential complex, a thermal complex was discovered to the east, and a building north of the main building may also have been used for residential purposes [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:103426", "url": "remediation_change_log", "q