ccording to the Historic Scotland information marker at the site, the southern circle''s first incarnation may have been constructed around 3000 BC [1]. The northern circle is smaller and consists of rounded river stones [1]. In its centre is a single stone; another stone is found on the edge of the circle [1]. This circle may have originated as a timber circle [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:155396", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-019: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/93/Temple_wood_2006.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/8ed8a300/Kilmartin Temple Wood Stone Circles 3.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:313955", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-009: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/8ed8a300/Kilmartin Temple Wood Stone Circles 3.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/8ed8a300/Temple_wood_2006.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('8f256d92-11a1-4310-90e2-be5cebfc350e'::uuid, 'mystery', '8', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:8f256d92-11a1-4310-90e2-be5cebfc350e:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''7'' restored on Great Serpent Mound', '23f7e10286e9de1ad55d6a8f181e5e96', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 8 from (''Mound/tumulus'', ''Undated'') is shared by 4 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:85970", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2129:chunk-0001: description ''The Great Serpent Mound is a 1,348-foot-long (411m), four-feet-high prehistoric effigy mound located in Peebles, Ohio[1]. It was built on the Serpent Mound crater plateau, running along Ohio Brush Creek in Adams County, Ohio[1]. The mound is the largest serpent effigy known in the world[1].'' -> ''The Great Serpent Mound is a 1,348-feet-long (411m), four-feet-high precontact effigy mound located in Peebles, Ohio, United States [1]. It was built on what is known as the Serpent Mound crater plateau, running along the Ohio Brush Creek in Adams County, Ohio [1]. The mound is the largest serpent effigy known in the world [1]. The first published surveys of the mound, by E. G. Squier and Edwin Hamilton Davis, were featured in their 1848 study Ancient Monuments of the Mississippi Valley [1]. Serpent Mound conforms to the surrounding land, as it was built on a bluff above the Ohio Brush Creek [1]. The mound is located on the site of a meteorite impact site known as the Serpent Mound crater [1]. The crater is around 8.7 miles in diameter and was formed 252–330 million years ago [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:120379", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s006: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:120380", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s006: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:155401", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-019: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/8f256d92/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/8f256d92/Adena Burial Mound at Serpent Mound.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:239749", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s006: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:239750", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s006: period_start None -> ''-300''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:313963", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-009: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/8f256d92/Adena Burial Mound at Serpent Mound.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/8f256d92/Serpent_mound_8438.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350876", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350877", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_start ''-300'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
