ithic engravings, as well as a cross, which is believed to have been carved in order to Christianise what was an ancient ritual [1]. It is considered a rare example of the veneration of stones associated with a secular, pagan fertility rite that has continued to the present [1]. The stone is more than two meters high, and has a shape similar to that of a mushroom, with the top having a circumference of about 7 meters [1]. The fertility rite involves girls of marriageable age consulting the rock to find out how long before they get married [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:121476", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s007: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:121477", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26b_fields-wd1-s007: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:156054", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-020: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2c/RochadosNamorados.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/940444fb/Menir da Rocha dos Namorados - Corval - Portugal (472182318).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251101", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s013: period_name None -> ''< 4500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251102", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s013: period_start None -> ''-10000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:323383", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-004-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/940444fb/Menir da Rocha dos Namorados - Corval - Portugal (472182318).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/940444fb/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:325304", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/940444fb/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/940444fb/RochadosNamorados.webp''"}, {"source": "r