cotzingo is claimed to be one of the first extant botanical gardens in the world, along with Moctezuma''s gardens in Huastepec [1]. The gardens and archaeological site are located roughly 20 miles northeast of central Mexico City, Mexico [1]. Texcotzingo is adjacent to the Aztec capital city of Texcoco and acted as the summer imperial gardens including imperial and courtly residences and fantastic waterworks [1]. Texcotzingo was designed and created by Nezahualcoyotl, the then-ruler of Texcoco, in the 15th century [1]. New hydraulic projects and terrace gardens transformed the previously un-arable land into lush edible gardens containing the three ubiquitous staples of the Americas: maize, beans, and squash [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:156142", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-020: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/80/El_invernadero_de_Nezahualcoyotl.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/972a2d53/Texcotzingo_Second_Level_View.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:314107", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-009: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/972a2d53/Texcotzingo_Second_Level_View.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/972a2d53/El_invernadero_de_Nezahualcoyotl.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('9737ca03-ad30-46d2-8740-3dec20bed1ea'::uuid, 'antiquity', '8', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:9737ca03-ad30-46d2-8740-3dec20bed1ea:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: antiquity ''5'' restored on Grakliani Hill', 'cf7242c8300e26e76e923ed91c6f0e8f', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 8 from period_start -4500"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:27264", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-21_mechanical-country: country ''Georgia (country)'' -> ''Georgia''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:36911", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0046:chunk-0001: description ''Grakliani Hill is a 7th-century BC temple complex in eastern Georgia near Kaspi, featuring a fertility goddess shrine with a disputed inscription that may predate other known regional scripts by over a millennium. Excavations revealed human presence potentially spanning 300,000 years [1].'' -> \"Grakliani Hill is an archaeological excavation site in eastern Georgia near Kaspi, showing evidence of human presence possibly going back 300,000 years [1]. The site was discovered in 2007, during work to widen the Tbilisi-Senaki-Leselidze highway [1]. The site contains a temple to a fertility goddess from the seventh century BCE, a pit-type burial cemetery from the early Bronze Age, and the remains of a building from around 450-350 BCE; the building consists of three rooms with three storage rooms [1]. The site had been occupied between the Chalcolithic and the Late Hellenistic periods [1]. The excavation of layers yielded artifacts including children''s toys, weapons, icons, and pharmacological devices [1]. Within the first two months of digging, archaeologists had excavated over 35,000 pieces from hundreds of graves and ruins of settlements that date back to the eighth century BCE [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:104246", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s014: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:104247", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s014: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:156681", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-021: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/9737ca03/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/9737ca03/Grakliani Gora archaeological site, Kaspi Municipality, Georgia 11.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251127", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s013: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251128", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s013: period_start None -> ''43''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:334618", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-009-002: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/9737ca03/Grakliani Gora archaeological site, Kaspi Municipality, Georgia 11.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/9737ca03/Grakliani_Script_(IX-X_century_B.D.).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:357269", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-25p_fields-wd5-s006: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:357270", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-25p_fields-wd5-s006: period_start ''43'' -> ''-4500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386595", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:386596", 