ly killed by diseases brought over by Europeans [1]. Large defensive ditches and palisades were built around some of the communities at Kuhikugu [1]. Many of the communities at Kuhikugu were linked, with roads which bridged some rivers along their paths, and with canoe canals running alongside some of the roads [1]. Sites X35 and X34 are significant communities connected by two of these roads [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105066", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s015: period_name ''500 - 1000 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105067", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s015: period_start ''500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:157562", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-022: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/a0b08567/hero.webp'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251523", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s014: period_name None -> ''500 - 1000 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:251524", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s014: period_start None -> ''500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350987", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_name ''500 - 1000 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:350988", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s006: period_start ''500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
