    ('a4990269-42fc-45f8-9849-905dbf3f68fb'::uuid, 'antiquity', '4', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:a4990269-42fc-45f8-9849-905dbf3f68fb:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: antiquity ''5'' restored on Anju Castle', '37bf7a502c09b9df725682950a1aa31f', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 4 from period_start -500"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:37037", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0049:chunk-0001: description ''Built between the 1st century BC and 7th century AD, Anju Castle is a multi-period fortress in Anju City, South Phyongan Province, North Korea [1]. Originally constructed during the Goguryeo kingdom as a northern defense point after the capital moved to Pyongyang, it was later rebuilt during the Joseon era [1].'' -> ''The Anju Castle is a military fortress built during the Goguryeo kingdom, later rebuilt during Joseon era [1]. It is located in Anju City, South Phyongan Province, North Korea [1]. The fortress consists of three parts, all built at different periods; an inner fort, an outer fort and a new fort [1]. The inner fort dates from the Goguryeo period; it has walls along the ridge of the Kadu range on the shore of the Chongchon River [1]. These walls were 7–8 metres high from the level ground and 4–5 metres on the slope of the hills, 6500 metres long [1]. The outer fort was built during Joseon period; it is 3 650 metres long [1]. The new fort is over 550 metres long and was built in the 17th century [1]. The fort was rebuilt several times during the Goryeo and the Joseon periods [1].''"}, {