    ('a6712eba-ba7a-4047-8462-0f4ae9343373'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:a6712eba-ba7a-4047-8462-0f4ae9343373:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''7'' restored on Grave Circle B, Mycenae', '82db4686575ce2a57484fbd0db5a52c6', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Cemetery'', ''3000 - 1500 BC'') is shared by 11 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:29610", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0314:chunk-0002: period_start ''-3000'' -> ''-1700''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:35930", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-25_mechanical-journal-reversal-3: period_start ''-1700'' -> ''-3000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:86538", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2145:chunk-0001: description ''A royal cemetery dating to roughly 1700-1600 BC, situated 117 metres west of the Lion Gate outside the Bronze Age citadel of Mycenae in southern Greece. The circle has a diameter of 28 metres and contains 26 graves -- 14 shaft graves and 12 cist graves -- enclosed by a circular stone wall. Discovered accidentally in 1951 during work on the nearby Tomb of Clytemnestra, it yielded bronze weapons and drinking vessels with male burials, and jewelry and ornaments with female burials. Skeletal analysis revealed many occupants were related and several males bore healed combat injuries, pointing to an elite warrior class.'' -> ''Grave Circle B in Mycenae is a 17th–16th century BCE royal cemetery situated outside the late Bronze Age citadel of Mycenae, southern Greece [1]. Grave Circle B, with a diameter of 28 m, is situated at a distance of 117 m west of the Lion Gate, the main entrance of Mycenae [1]. The Circle hosts a total of 26 graves; 14 of which are shaft graves and the rest simple cists [1]. A total of 24 persons were found in the shafts, while six of the shaft graves were family tombs in which several occupants were found [1]. The women in the graves were richly dressed and decorated with various ornaments, such as earrings, necklaces, bands of gold and silver pins [1]. A death mask of electrum has been also unearthed [1]. The burial complex was discovered in 1951 by accident, when workmen were digging at a nearby 13th century BCE tholos tomb [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:158265", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-023: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/a6712eba/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/a6712eba/Grave_circle_B_1.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
