94 BCE and was subsequently reinforced by Roman walls [1]. An ancient Roman temple dating from this time was reconstructed as a temple for Augustus in the 1st century CE in the centre of the fortress [1]. The temple was later converted into the Pozzuoli Cathedral which stands to this day [1]. Rione Terra was populated until 1970 when it was evacuated due to a sudden bradyseism event that raised the hill on which the district is located by 1.7 m relative to sea level [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:158441", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-023: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2e/Rione_Terra_visto_dal_porto_di_Pozzuoli_%282010%29_by_RaBoe-22.jpg'' -> \"/data/images/wiki/ab336181/L''antico decumano sepolto.webp\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:315673", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-011: thumbnail_url \"/data/images/wiki/ab336181/L''antico decumano sepolto.webp\" -> ''/data/images/wiki/ab336181/Rione_Terra_visto_dal_porto_di_Pozzuoli_(2010)_by_RaBoe-22.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
