he fortress became the Roman colony of Puteoli in 194 BCE and was subsequently reinforced by Roman walls [1]. An ancient Roman temple dating from this time was reconstructed as a temple for Augustus in the 1st century CE in the centre of the fortress [1]. The temple was later converted into the Pozzuoli Cathedral which stands to this day [1]. Rione Terra was populated until 1970 when it was evacuated due to a sudden bradyseism event that raised the hill on which the district is located by 1.7 m relative to sea level [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:158441", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-023: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2e/Rione_Terra_visto_dal_porto_di_Pozzuoli_%282010%29_by_RaBoe-22.jpg'' -> \"/data/images/wiki/ab336181/L''antico decumano sepolto.webp\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:315673", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-011: thumbnail_url \"/data/images/wiki/ab336181/L''antico decumano sepolto.webp\" -> ''/data/images/wiki/ab336181/Rione_Terra_visto_dal_porto_di_Pozzuoli_(2010)_by_RaBoe-22.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('ac94e596-0960-45e2-acc5-bba445decae9'::uuid, 'mystery', '1', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:ac94e596-0960-45e2-acc5-bba445decae9:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''4'' restored on Castell Cawr', '0c69072bb6be3f811c0d5f33f2d050f2', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 1 from (''Fortress/citadel'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 235 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:86684", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2149:chunk-0001: description ''(1500–500 BC) Castell Cawr is an Iron Age hillfort on the 189-metre hill of Tan-y-Gopa above Abergele, overlooking the River Clwyd [1]. The massive hillfort crowns an isolated hill on the escarpment above the coastal levels [2]. Today the heavily forested site is owned by the Woodland Trust and supports rare lesser horseshoe bats in caves within the hill [1]. The location offers extensive views to Snowdonia and the Clwydian Range [1].'' -> ''Castell Cawr, or Tan-y-Gopa as it is known locally, is a heavily forested hill above the town of Abergele in Conwy county borough, Wales [1]. On it is found the Iron Age hillfort of Castell Cawr, which overlooks the River Clwyd [1]. The hill rises to 189 m (620 ft) above sea level [1]. Thomas Pennant visited the area in the 18th century, and noted the existence of the hillfort [1]. In 1860, James Halliwell-Phillipps wrote that the outline of the hillfort was obscured by vegetation, and identified the workings of a Roman lead mine on the hillside [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105940", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s016: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105941", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s016: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:241670", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s008: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:241671", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s008: period_start None -> ''-800''"}]'::jsonb),
