c circles, diamond patterns, and inscriptions, exhibit remarkable realism and energy [1]. The Bangudae rocks are around 8 m wide and around 5 m high [1]. In total, 312 engravings can be seen, of which 200 figures are accounted for as the animals and 23 are unidentified creatures [1]. Animals whose species can be identified include large cetaceans such as the northern right whale, the humpback whale, the right whale, the gray whale, and the sperm whale [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:158508", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-023: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/ad2b103b/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/ad2b103b/울주 대곡리 반구대 암각화.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('ad2eb54f-98a3-4299-8cd5-56e3ddc0b48f'::uuid, 'mystery', '4', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:ad2eb54f-98a3-4299-8cd5-56e3ddc0b48f:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''5'' restored on Temple E, Selinus', '868f028a99a6c15c6966c7f71db35fbe', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 4 from (''Temple complex'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 53 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:86708", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2150:chunk-0001: description ''Temple E at Selinus is a Doric Greek temple in Sicily, one of the best-preserved structures at this Magna Graecia city. Located on the hill east of the acropolis, it was constructed towards the middle of the 5th century BC atop earlier foundations. An inscription on a votive stela indicates dedication to Hera, though some scholars propose Aphrodite based on structural parallels. Its current appearance results from controversial anastylosis in 1959 by Italian archaeologist Jole Bovio Marconi. [1]'' -> \"Temple E at Selinus in Sicily is a Greek temple of Magna Graecia of the Doric order [1]. It is found on the hill to the east of the city''s acropolis [1]. Temple E is also known as the Temple of Hera because an inscription found on a votive stela indicates that it was dedicated to Hera; however, some scholars argue that it must have been dedicated to Aphrodite on the basis of structural parallels [1]. It was built towards the middle of the fifth century BC on top of the foundations of a more ancient building [1]. It is the best conserved of the temples of Selinus but its present appearance is the result of anastylosis (reconstruction using original material) performed—controversially—in 1959 [1]. The peripteral temple belongs to the period of transition from the archaic to the classical period [1]. It has a peristyle 25.33 wide x 67.82 metres long with six columns at the front and fifteen on the long sides [1]. The columns are each 10.19 metres high with numerous traces of the stucco which originally covered them [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105964", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s016: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:105965", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s016: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:158509", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-023: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b1/Sicily_Selinunte_Temple_E_%28Hera%29.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/ad2eb54f/91022 Marinella di Selinunte, Province of Trapani, Italy - panoramio (13).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:241687", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s008: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:241688", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s008: period_start None -> ''-450''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:315705", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-011: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/ad2eb54f/91022 Marinella di Selinunte, Province of Trapani, Italy - panoramio (13).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/ad2eb54f/Sicily_Selinunte_Temple_E_(Hera).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
