 — including scrapers, awls, and blades — as well as a quantity of pottery fragments, confirming a date in the Copper Age of the fourth millennium BC [1]. Further documented finds at the site include obsidian stones, sandstone vessels, burnt ornaments, necklaces, and beads of metal, shell, and bone, alongside fan scrapers [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:159155", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-024: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/b0a89bee/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/b0a89bee/Rajajil standing columns, al-Jouf, 6th - 5th millenia BCE (1).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:315767", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-011: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/b0a89bee/Rajajil standing columns, al-Jouf, 6th - 5th millenia BCE (1).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/b0a89bee/أعمدة_الرجاجيل_2.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
