 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:106853", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s017: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:106854", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s017: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:106855", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s017: site_type ''Stone circle'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:241797", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s008: site_type None -> ''Stone circle''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252407", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s016: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252408", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s016: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:351894", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s007: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:351895", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s007: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:401257", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:401258", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s003: period_start None -> ''-4500''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('b7cc5073-ffca-4cd3-a168-3062908d4959'::uuid, 'mystery', '1', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:b7cc5073-ffca-4cd3-a168-3062908d4959:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''4'' restored on Beacon Hill, West Sussex', '54f1b26b8253e71e970f7764dd786900', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 1 from (''Fortress/citadel'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 235 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:87000", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2158:chunk-0001: description ''Beacon Hill, also known as Harting Beacon, is a hillfort on the South Downs in West Sussex, England [1]. Located in the parish of Elsted and Treyford within Chichester District, the hilltop enclosure dates to the Late Bronze Age, from the 8th to the 6th centuries BC [1]. The hillfort defences were renewed during the Late Iron Age [1]. The site is a Scheduled Ancient Monument [1].'' -> ''Beacon Hill, also known as Harting Beacon, is a hillfort on the South Downs, in the county of West Sussex in southern England [1]. The hilltop enclosure is dated to the Late Bronze Age, from the 8th to 6th centuries BC [1]. The hillfort defences were renewed during the Late Iron Age [1]. The fort extends approximately 400 metres east-west by approximately 500 metres north-south, and covers an area of approximately 10 hectares [1]. Archaeological investigations of the hillfort took place from 1948 to 1952, and from 1976 to 1977 [1]. As well as the Bronze Age remains, the area of the fort also includes an Anglo-Saxon burial mound, and the foundations of a late 18th-century telegraph station [1]. The hillfort is situated on the top of the hill and is defined by a single rampart and a flat-bottomed ditch, which survives as a low bank up to 6 metres wide [1]. The rampart was originally faced with timber, with timber palisades acting as retaining walls on both the inside and the outside [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:160021", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-025: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/b7cc5073/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/b7cc5073/Beacon_Hill_fort_1.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
