med after Cenwalh of Wessex [1]. The site straddles the modern border between Somerset and Wiltshire, and is within Castle Wood which covers its defences and interior [1]. The latter has an area of 1.6 hectares [1]. There is a single rampart and ditch which are well preserved in places [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:106950", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s017: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:106951", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s017: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:160678", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-026: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/bc936eb9/hero.webp'' -> \"/data/images/wiki/bc936eb9/Kenwalch''s_Castle_earthworks.webp\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252785", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:252786", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s017: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387322", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387323", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
