external colonnade has eight fluted columns at the front and rear and seventeen columns on each of the long sides [1]. The first excavations were undertaken by Robert Murdoch Smith and E. A. Porcher in 1861 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107004", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s017: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107005", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s017: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:242705", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s009: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:242706", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s009: period_start None -> ''-500''"}]'::jsonb),
