    ('c548194d-9265-44f0-bba7-13fa0f9835a8'::uuid, 'mystery', '1', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:c548194d-9265-44f0-bba7-13fa0f9835a8:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''4'' restored on Citânia de Santa Luzia', '8f0971c48a681229749ac725db42aa77', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 1 from (''Fortress/citadel'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 235 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:37475", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0056:chunk-0001: description ''The Citânia de Santa Luzia is a fortified Castro culture settlement in Areosa, Viana do Castelo, Portugal, dating from the Iron Age with continued Roman-period occupation[1]. First excavated in 1876 by Joaquim Possidonio Narciso da Silva, only about one third of its structures have been uncovered[1]. The remaining portion lies beneath or was destroyed during construction of nearby hotels, churches, and roads[1]. A medieval chapel dedicated to Saint Lucy once marked the site until 1926, when it was demolished to make way for a new church designed by Miguel Ventura Terra[1].'' -> \"The Citânia de Santa Luzia is an archaeological site of the Castro culture located in the Portuguese civil parish of Areosa in the municipality of Viana do Castelo [1]. Its construction dates from the Iron Age, and it shows evidence of occupation during the Roman period [1]. The Castro was first dug in 1876 by Joaquim Possidonio Narciso da Silva [1]. The Citânia was constructed on the top of the Santa Luzia hill, overseeing the Lima River''s delta and is protected by three lines of walls, towers, and two moats [1]. The innermost walls enclose a 30m by 20m area that contains a single circular house and its only entrance faces West [1]. Ruins of approximately 74 houses have been found [1]. Most of them have circular foundations or elliptical, and few are rectangular [1]. The findings of the Citânia de Santa Luzia include multiple ceramics of the Castro, Roman, and Visigothic eras [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107995", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107996", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_start ''-3000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:161471", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-027: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c548194d/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c548194d/Citânia de Santa Luzia - Viana do Castelo - Portugal (5051353293).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:242774", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s009: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:242775", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s009: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:316750", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-012: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c548194d/Citânia de Santa Luzia - Viana do Castelo - Portugal (5051353293).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c548194d/Citânia_de_Santa_Luzia_-_Viana_do_Castelo_-_Portugal_(6649483995).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
