ma River''s delta and is protected by three lines of walls, towers, and two moats [1]. The innermost walls enclose a 30m by 20m area that contains a single circular house and its only entrance faces West [1]. Ruins of approximately 74 houses have been found [1]. Most of them have circular foundations or elliptical, and few are rectangular [1]. The findings of the Citânia de Santa Luzia include multiple ceramics of the Castro, Roman, and Visigothic eras [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107995", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:107996", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_start ''-3000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:161471", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-027: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c548194d/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c548194d/Citânia de Santa Luzia - Viana do Castelo - Portugal (5051353293).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:242774", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s009: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:242775", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s009: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:316750", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-012: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c548194d/Citânia de Santa Luzia - Viana do Castelo - Portugal (5051353293).webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c548194d/Citânia_de_Santa_Luzia_-_Viana_do_Castelo_-_Portugal_(6649483995).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('c5d2dfc5-1a50-4b7c-a3f1-6879aa5b1c67'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:c5d2dfc5-1a50-4b7c-a3f1-6879aa5b1c67:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''5'' restored on Castlenalacht Stone Row', 'cf60356bdc736d852cf3ce65b620f442', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Megalithic stones'', ''Undated'') is shared by 25 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:87344", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2169:chunk-0001: description ''Castlenalacht Stone Row is an alignment of four tall free-standing stones on a hilltop in the townland of Castlenalacht, 6 km north of Bandon, County Cork, Ireland. Dating from the Bronze Age (c. 3,000-4,000 years ago), it is the largest of over 80 stone rows in south-west Ireland, with the tallest stone reaching 3.4 metres high. The stones are arranged in ascending height order across 13.4 metres on a north-east/south-west axis, with the largest stone at the south-east end. Like other Irish stone rows, the builders favoured hilltop locations where the axis points toward a distant horizon more than 5 km away. The precise function is unknown, though most archaeologists assume a ceremonial or ritualistic purpose.'' -> \"Castlenalacht Stone Row is an alignment of four tall and free-standing stones located on a hilltop in the townland of Castlenalacht, Innishannon parish, 6 km north of Bandon, County Cork [1]. It dates from the Bronze Age (c. 3000–4000 years ago) and is the largest of the over 80 stone rows in south-west Ireland [1]. The four Castlenalacht stones are arranged in ascending order of height across a distance of 13.4 m [1]. The site is placed on one of the area''s highest hilltops; according to the archaeologist Clive Ruggles, the builders tended to favour locations where the axis, from largest to smallest stone, leads to a relatively distant horizon [1]. The precise functions of these constructions are unknown; most archaeologists assume a ceremonial or ritualistic purpose [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108010", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108011", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_start ''-2000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:161485", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-027: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c5d2dfc5/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c5d2dfc5/Castlenalacht5.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253189", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s018: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253190", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s018: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352763", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352764", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387362", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387363", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_start ''-2500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
