 south-west Ireland [1]. The four Castlenalacht stones are arranged in ascending order of height across a distance of 13.4 m [1]. The site is placed on one of the area''s highest hilltops; according to the archaeologist Clive Ruggles, the builders tended to favour locations where the axis, from largest to smallest stone, leads to a relatively distant horizon [1]. The precise functions of these constructions are unknown; most archaeologists assume a ceremonial or ritualistic purpose [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108010", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108011", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_start ''-2000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:161485", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-027: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c5d2dfc5/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c5d2dfc5/Castlenalacht5.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253189", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s018: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253190", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s018: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352763", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352764", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387362", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387363", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_start ''-2500'' -> None"}]