, near the entrance [1]. The hillfort was investigated in 1849 by W. Wynne-Ffoulkes [1]. He dug a number of small trenches and concluded that the eastern entrance had been paved and that the inner rampart was built of stone or fronted with stone [1]. In 2007, a topographic survey was carried out for the Heather and Hillforts Project [1]. The survey identified 15 roundhouse platforms within the enclosure, along with possible evidence that the inner rampart was faced with stone at some time during the site''s occupation [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108029", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108030", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_start ''-1500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:161532", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-027: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Moel-y-Gaer,_Llanbedr_Dyffryn_Clwyd_yng_Nghesail_Moel_Famau_-_Moel_y_Gaer,_Clwydian_Hills_in_the_country_of_Wales_27.jpg/400px-Moel-y-Gaer,_Llanbedr_Dyffryn_Clwyd_yng_Nghesail_Moel_Famau_-_Moel_y_Gaer,_Clwydian_Hills_in_the_country_of_Wales_27.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c6ad2aac/Moel-y-Gaer, Llanbedr Dyffryn Clwyd yng Nghesail Moel Famau - Moel y Gaer, Clwydian Hills in the country of Wales 27.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253199", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s018: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253200", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s018: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387364", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387365", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quot