ft high is the largest on Dartmoor, was re-erected by Sabine Baring-Gould, R. Hansford Worth and others in 1893 [1]. Drizzlecombe is located on the western side of Dartmoor, about 4 miles east of the village of Yelverton, to the west of the upper reaches of the River Plym [1]. Nearby is the large but damaged cairn known as Giant''s Basin; many of its stones were removed by warreners to build their rabbit-warrens at Ditsworthy, lower down the river [1]. Higher up the slope and overlooking these monuments is a village of stone hut circles [1].\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108045", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108046", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s018: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:161575", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-027: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c82e8c63/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c82e8c63/Drizzlecombe kist 1.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253211", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s018: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253212", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s018: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:317409", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c82e8c63/Drizzlecombe kist 1.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/c82e8c63/Drizzlecombe_large_stone.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352782", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''3000 - 1500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352783", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_start ''-4000'' -> ''-2500''"}, {"source": "remed