rthern edge, which may have been an entrance [1]. Castlerigg stone circle was one of the monuments included in the Ancient Monuments Protection Act 1882 [1]. It thus became one of the first scheduled monuments [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:162091", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-028: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/c8ec86a6/hero.webp'' -> \"/data/images/wiki/c8ec86a6/1011362 Castlerigg stone circle St. John''s Castlerigg and Wythburn 20240526 0001.webp\""}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:332941", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-006-002: thumbnail_url \"/data/images/wiki/c8ec86a6/1011362 Castlerigg stone circle St. John''s Castlerigg and Wythburn 20240526 0001.webp\" -> ''/data/images/wiki/c8ec86a6/Castlerigg Stone Circle.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
