    ('ccb5fcce-35d3-463a-bb98-0cfc09918465'::uuid, 'mystery', '1', '4', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:ccb5fcce-35d3-463a-bb98-0cfc09918465:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''4'' restored on Castro of Cidadelhe', 'ab3ae0986dc54fab595856de1c202ea2', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 1 from (''Fortress/citadel'', ''1500 - 500 BC'') is shared by 235 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:42088", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0059:chunk-0001: description ''The Castro of Cidadelhe is a fortified settlement in Mesao Frio, Vila Real district, Portugal, with proto-historic origins and subsequent Roman and Medieval occupation. Founded as a metallurgical settlement during the Late Bronze Age (8th-9th century BC), it was destroyed and later reoccupied during the Castro culture period. The site features five concentric defensive wall circuits adapted to the terrain. Known historically as Civitadella, it was destroyed in 134 BC by Roman forces. A medieval quadrangular tower from the 10th century stands in the acropolis area. The Roman military road from Braga to Amarante passed through the parish, and traces of Roman presence include a stretch of paved road and the Martinhos Bridge.'' -> ''The Castro of Cidadelhe is a Portuguese castro in civil parish of Cidadelhe, in the municipality of Mesão Frio [1]. Cidadelhe was a fortified settlement of a proto-historic nature, later occupied by Roman and Medieval residents [1]. The castro is located in an isolated rural environment on a hilltop [1]. Two lines of walls encircle the castle and roadways/paths, composed of schist rock [1]. In the interior of the ruins are several remains of residences, of a circular design, excavated by recent archaeologists [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108789", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108790", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_start ''-3000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243655", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243656", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_start None -> ''-900''"}]'::jsonb),
