o the back and front [1]. The hill has a summit of 141 m AOD, and is a prominent landmark rising above the Cheshire Plain [1]. The hill fort is protected as a Scheduled Ancient Monument [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108828", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108829", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_start ''-1000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243673", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:243674", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-02b_fields-wd3-s010: period_start None -> ''-1250''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:317552", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-013: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/ce525bf9/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/ce525bf9/Helsby, The Hill in the Snow - geograph.org.uk - 208875.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
