ing [1]. A second stone is 1.0 metres high and appears to have had its top broken off [1]. A third stone is 1.3 metres high but has been roughly squared off and is currently being used as a gate post [1]. A fourth stone, 1.4 metres high, is found in an old field bank and is much-weathered and leaning [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108854", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108855", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253621", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s019: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253622", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s019: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352843", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:352844", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s008: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('d0e007ba-24cd-4929-b135-0b907397e531'::uuid, 'antiquity', '8', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:d0e007ba-24cd-4929-b135-0b907397e531:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: antiquity ''5'' restored on Long Low, Wetton', '1ad1b0ba44d49b11f8ac6af1f95552fa', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 8 from period_start -4500"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:42124", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0060:chunk-0001: description ''Long Low is a Neolithic and Bronze Age site about 2 km southeast of Wetton in Staffordshire, consisting of two round cairns linked by a connecting bank -- a layout unique in England. The northern cairn is 23 metres in diameter and 2.4 metres high. Excavated between 1846 and 1851, the primary chamber yielded remains of at least 13 individuals along with three finely chipped flint arrowheads and animal bones. The connecting ridge contained scattered human bone fragments and charcoal, suggesting prolonged funerary use spanning the late Neolithic to Bronze Age.'' -> ''Long Low is a Neolithic and Bronze Age site in the English county of Staffordshire [1]. It is about 2 km SE of Wetton [1]. It consists of two round cairns linked by a connecting bank – an unusual layout and one that is unique in England [1]. The northern cairn measures 23 metres in diameter and survives to a height of 2.4 metres [1]. It appears to be related to other chamber tombs of the Peak District group and was excavated by Samuel Carrington in 1849 [1]. Carrington found a burial chamber built from limestone orthostats with a paved floor [1]. The bones of thirteen individuals were recovered as well as three leaf-shaped flint arrowheads [1]. The smaller southern cairn is 15 metres across and survives to 1.2 metres in height following extensive modern damage [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108856", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:108857", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s019: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253623", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s019: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:253624", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s019: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387400", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:387401", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:401859", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:401860", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_start None -> ''-4500''"}]'::jsonb),
