s, when it could have been part of the programme of works instigated by Pericles [1]. The Erechtheion is unique in the corpus of Greek temples in that its asymmetrical composition does not conform to the canon of Greek classical architecture [1]. The classical Erechtheion is the last in a series of buildings approximately on the mid-north site of the Acropolis of Athens, the earliest of which dates back to the late Bronze Age Mycenaean period [1]. The entablature of the naos and north porch has a frieze of blue Eleusinian limestone that was decorated with white Pentelic marble figures attached by means of iron dowels [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:164322", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-031: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/dcb2c5f2/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/dcb2c5f2/1027 Porch of the Maidens of the Erechtheion at Acropolis of Athens Photo by Giles Laurent.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:318421", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/dcb2c5f2/1027 Porch of the Maidens of the Erechtheion at Acropolis of Athens Photo by Giles Laurent.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/dcb2c5f2/Erechtheum_Acropolis_Athens.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
    ('dce4d9db-1bf4-4430-b5e6-2e13e63e4813'::uuid, 'mystery', '6', '7', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:dce4d9db-1bf4-4430-b5e6-2e13e63e4813:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''7'' restored on Verziau of Gargantua', '53ee21e86723b01622e4b58e995942e6', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 6 from (''Megalithic stones'', ''< 4500 BC'') is shared by 12 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:87892", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2185:chunk-0001: description ''The Verziau of Gargantua, also known as Haute-Borne, is a prehistoric menhir at Bois-les-Pargny in the Aisne department, northern France. The monolith stands 4.35 meters high and 1.50 meters wide at its base, tapering to just over 1 meter at the top, carved from locally sourced hard sandstone. First documented by Amedee Piette in 1851, it was classified as a Historic Monument in 1889. A twin menhir once stood nearby but was destroyed in the early 19th century for its stone. According to local Picard legend, a giant used the stone -- called a verziau -- to sharpen his scythe and left it on the hillside in a gesture of anger.'' -> ''The verziau of Gargantua (or vierzeux of Gargantua), also known as Haute-Borne, is a menhir at Bois-lès-Pargny in Aisne, France [1]. The menhir is north of the town of Bois-lès-Pargny, a few meters from a small copse, near Sons-et-Ronchères [1]. At the beginning of the 19th century, the menhir had a twin sister, which was destroyed to extract a large amount of sandstone [1]. Legend has it that a man of immense size was using it to sharpen his scythe, and left the rock on the site in a gesture of anger [1]. The monument was listed as a monument historique in 1889 [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:109797", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s020: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:109798", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s020: period_start ''-4500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:164323", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-031: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a1/Verziau_de_Gargantua%2C_Bois-l%C3%A8s-Pargny.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/dce4d9db/Verziau de Gargantua 2.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254127", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_name None -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254128", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:318424", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/dce4d9db/Verziau de Gargantua 2.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/dce4d9db/Verziau_de_Gargantua,_Bois-lès-Pargny.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353733", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_name ''4500 - 3000 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353734", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_start ''-4000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:354795", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-19r_fields-wd5-s001: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''4500 - 3000 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:354796", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-19r_fields-wd5-s001: period_start None -> ''-4000''"}, {"source": "remediation_c