    ('e2574770-baac-4cba-a7c3-16e5b2650f8d'::uuid, 'mystery', '4', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:e2574770-baac-4cba-a7c3-16e5b2650f8d:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''5'' restored on Cerro de los Santos', 'b072f48f3fa0e9cca89a05afb4e61313', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 4 from (''Temple complex'', ''500 BC - 1 AD'') is shared by 53 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:88048", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2189:chunk-0001: description ''Cerro de los Santos is an Iberian religious sanctuary built in the 4th century BCE, located in southeastern Spain [1]. The site lies beside an ancient road and was used from the Iberian period through Roman times [1]. Little remains of the original temple structure, though 19th-century excavations documented its layout [1]. The sanctuary is renowned for approximately 300 votive sculptures, the majority depicting women, including the famous Dama del Cerro de los Santos [1].'' -> ''Cerro de los Santos is an Iberian religious sanctuary built in the 4th century BCE with evidence of continued use into the Roman period [1]. The site is known for its many votive sculptures, numbering about 300 [1]. Most of the sculptures depict women including the most notable find, the Dama del Cerro de los Santos [1]. In addition to the women, statues of men, possibly dating from a later period, and a few statues of animals have also been found [1]. The site is located outside of the municipality of Montealegre del Castillo in the province of Albacete, Spain [1]. The sculptures accumulated over time with the earliest being dated to the 4th century BCE while later examples have Latin letter inscriptions or appear more Roman in style [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:164502", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-031: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e2574770/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e2574770/Cabeza masculina ibérica - MAC.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:318519", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e2574770/Cabeza masculina ibérica - MAC.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e2574770/Dama_oferente_del_Cerro_de_los_Santos_(16119971754).webp''"}]'::jsonb),
