 1840, perhaps in 1848, during the construction of the railway which used to link the mines from Bert to Dompierre-sur-Besbre [1]. A third cave (today collapsed), was discovered in 1867 by Bailleau [1]. Several thousand flint blades and mammoth tusks of over 2 metres (6 ft 7 in) long were found [1]. The last research, from 1951 to 1954 and in 1962, was led by Henri Delporte and revealed back blades of flint, burins, drills and scrapers [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110549", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110550", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:164508", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-031: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e2a08d7d/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e2a08d7d/Upper Paleolithic scrapers Wellcome M0015595.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254175", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254176", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:326312", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-06-005-003: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e2a08d7d/Upper Paleolithic scrapers Wellcome M0015595.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e2a08d7d/Châtelperron - grotte des fées - 2.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353756", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353757", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
    ('e2aa3754-8d32-4455-bf6d-9077f18d50d2'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '2', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:e2aa3754-8d32-4455-bf6d-9077f18d50d2:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''2'' restored on Ancient Lilaia', '66ead504d0b56dcba7daeb3f776077eb', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''Undated'') is shared by 120 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:28536", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase3:batch-0155:chunk-0003: site_type ''Temple complex'' -> ''City/town/settlement''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81386", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2031:chunk-0001: description \"Ruins of an important Phocian city in central Greece, inhabited since the 3rd millennium BC and named after the nymph Lilaia, daughter of the river god Cephissus. Listed in Homer''s Iliad among nine Phocian towns that sent warriors to Troy. Its fortification walls were destroyed by Philip II of Macedon in 346 BC and later rebuilt. Pausanias recorded a theatre, agora, baths, and temples of Apollo and Artemis at the site. The springs of the Cephissus River rise nearby.\" -> ''Lilaea or Lilaia, also Lilaeum or Lilaion, was one of the most important ancient Phocian towns, and a polis, built on the north slopes of Mount Parnassus, and at the sources of the Cephissus [1]. The name Lilaea appears for the first time in Homer\\''s Iliad as one of the nine Phocian towns which had participated at the Trojan War [1]. The broader region of Lilaea had been inhabited since the 3rd millennium BCE [1]. Lilaea was destroyed during the Third Sacred War by Philip II of Macedon in 346 BCE, but it was rebuilt during the following years in the course of the project for the reconstruction of the Phocian citadels [1]. When Pausanias visited Lilaea, in the second century, he reported seeing a theatre, an agora, and baths, with temples of Apollo and Artemis [1]. Lilaea is located near the modern namesake village of Lilaia [1]. Its walls and gates are to the east of the modern settlement [1]. The fortification of the city is evident on the hill \"Pyrgos\" or \"Palaeokastro\" [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110551", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_name ''3000 - 1500 BC'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110552", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_start ''-3000'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:164509", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-031: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e2aa3754/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e2aa3754/Acropolis of Lilaia 3.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254177", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_name None -> ''500 BC - 1 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254178", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_start None -> ''-500''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353758", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353759", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}]'::jsonb),
