    ('e355bfda-5a11-4b50-813f-8212abdd0009'::uuid, 'antiquity', '7', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:e355bfda-5a11-4b50-813f-8212abdd0009:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: antiquity ''5'' restored on Tischofer Cave', '6620514bae3791a6c90b4a157b863922', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 7 from period_start -3000"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:81388", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2031:chunk-0001: description ''The Tischofer Cave is a cave in the Kaisertal valley in the Kaisergebirge mountains of Austria. The roughly 40 metre long cave, about 8.5 metres high at the entrance, was occupied by cave bears during the Paleolithic as evidenced by numerous excavated skeletal remains [1]. Bone tools made of cave bear bones and skulls, dated to about 27,000–28,000 years ago, were discovered here [1]. This makes the Tischofer Cave the oldest known uncontested site of human occupation in Tyrol [1]. The cave also served as a locally important gathering place and weapons cache during the Tyrolean Rebellion in the Napoleonic Wars [1].'' -> ''The Tischofer Cave is a cave in the Kaisertal valley in the Kaisergebirge mountains in Austria [1]. The roughly 40 m long cave, which is about 8.5 m high at the entrance, was occupied by cave bears and other predators as shelter during the Paleolithic as evidenced by numerous excavated skeletal remains [1]. Bone tools of paleo-human inhabitants made of cave bear bones and skulls discovered here and dated to about 27,000 - 28,000 years ago may be viewed in the local history mus