    ('e4b003f4-3f62-4689-9af9-4b7f120614af'::uuid, 'mystery', '3', '2', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:e4b003f4-3f62-4689-9af9-4b7f120614af:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''2'' restored on Navalia', '5ab3651f39010b2ecf629fee1b461786', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 3 from (''City/town/settlement'', ''Undated'') is shared by 120 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:88096", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2190:chunk-0001: description ''Navalia was an ancient settlement mentioned by the Greek geographer Claudius Ptolemy in his 2nd-century AD Geographia. The name derives from the Latin word for \"dock\" or \"wharf\", though this meaning may be coincidental. Recent scholarship has tentatively identified the settlement with the area near modern-day Essen, Germany. Ptolemy provided coordinates, but the exact prime meridian he used remains unknown, and the coordinates have been corrupted by errors in medieval manuscript copies, making precise localization difficult.'' -> ''Navalia is a town (polis or oppidum) that was mentioned by Claudius Ptolemaeus in his Geographia [1]. The town has recently been associated with Essen [1]. The name translates from Latin as \"dock\" or \"wharf\", but this may be coincidental [1]. Though Ptolemy provides coordinates, it is unknown which prime meridian he used [1]. Moreover the coordinates provided have been polluted by mistakes by copyists [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110578", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1