hat formed the urban area [1]. The ground arch spanned the stream on a length of some 100 m, giving the bridge the appearance of a tube or a tunnel, although it was constructed entirely above ground [1]. It consists of a single, 5.7 m wide vault whose uphill mouth widens to 7 m [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110603", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:110604", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s021: period_start ''1'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165075", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-032: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c7/The_late_imperial_Roman_bridge%2C_the_100_m_%28328_ft%29_long_substructure_was_the_second_largest_of_its_kind_in_antiquity_after_the_Pergamon_Bridge%2C_Nysa_on_the_Meander%2C_Turkey_%2820254375673%29.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e62c980a/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254207", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_name None -> ''1 - 500 AD''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:254208", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s020: period_start None -> ''43''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:318598", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-014: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e62c980a/hero.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e62c980a/The_late_imperial_Roman_bridge,_the_100_m_(328_ft)_long_substructure_was_the_second_largest_of_its_kind_in_antiquity_after_the_Pergamon_Bridge,_Nysa_on_the_Meander,_Turkey_(20254375673).webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353777", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s009: period_name ''1 - 500 AD'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:353778", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s0