ssed perimeter walls, massive gates, a parade ground within its walls, and storage rooms that entirely occupied the ground floor [1]. The city of Teishebaini was built by Rusa II in mid-7th century BC to protect the eastern borders of Urartu from the barbaric Cimmerians and Scythians [1]. Within the city was a governors palace that contained a hundred and twenty rooms spreading across more than 40,000 m2, and citadel named the Citadel of Teisheba after the Urartian god of war [1]. The palace was made of stone, with timber ceilings, and timber columns that supported the roof [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:165081", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-032: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/95/Karmir_Blur_Hill.JPG'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e6b17dcc/Teishebaini_04.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:319205", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "import-hero-2026-10-05-002-015: thumbnail_url ''/data/images/wiki/e6b17dcc/Teishebaini_04.webp'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/e6b17dcc/Karmir_Blur_Hill.webp''"}]'::jsonb),
