    ('f9f8e1fa-4460-419a-97cf-1e0e2fb6a565'::uuid, 'antiquity', '6', '5', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:f9f8e1fa-4460-419a-97cf-1e0e2fb6a565:antiquity', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: antiquity ''5'' restored on Xyniae', '1b504ee4f7711cf377a7c71f266057e5', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "antiquity = 6 from period_start -1500"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:43247", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-0069:chunk-0001: description ''Xyniae was an ancient city in Achaea Phthiotis, Thessaly, Greece, strategically positioned on a promontory in Lake Xynias on the western slopes of Mount Othrys. It controlled vital passages from Lamia to Thaumaci (modern Domokos). The city changed hands repeatedly: Aetolian in the late 3rd century BC, then Macedonian, before being plundered and its population massacred by Aetolians in 198 BC. Roman general Flamininus reached Xyniae after a three-day march from Heraclea in 197 BC. Known as Ezeros in the Middle Ages, the ancient site is marked by ruined structures on a peninsula in the lake near modern Xyniada.'' -> ''Xyniae or Xyniai or Xynia was an ancient city in Achaea Phthiotis, Ancient Thessaly, in Greece [1]. The city was located on the western slopes of Mount Othrys, some 4 km southwest of the modern village of Xyniada (in the Phthiotis Prefecture) [1]. The city was strategically located as it controlled the passages along the nearby Lake Xynias (the lake took its name from the city), from Lamia to Thaumaci (modern Domokos) [1]. During the second half of the 3rd century BC the city was Aetolian, but passed to Macedonia after that, only to be plundered and its population massacred by the Aetolians in 198 BC [1]. In 186/5 BC it passed under Thessalian control, and then under Roman rule [1]. A castle was built amidst the ruins of the ancient acropolis; in part its outer walls follow the ancient foundations, but overall it encloses a much smaller space than the ancient fortifications [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:112274", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s023: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:112275", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s023: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:166768", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-034: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Ancient_Xyniai.jpg/400px-Ancient_Xyniai.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/f9f8e1fa/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:255061", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s022: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:255062", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s022: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:354442", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s010: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:354443", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s010: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:401983", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:401984", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_start None -> ''-1500''"}]'::jsonb),
