tury BC the city was Aetolian, but passed to Macedonia after that, only to be plundered and its population massacred by the Aetolians in 198 BC [1]. In 186/5 BC it passed under Thessalian control, and then under Roman rule [1]. A castle was built amidst the ruins of the ancient acropolis; in part its outer walls follow the ancient foundations, but overall it encloses a much smaller space than the ancient fortifications [1].''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:112274", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s023: period_name ''500 BC - 1 AD'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:112275", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-09-26d_fields-wd1-s023: period_start ''-500'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:166768", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "served-image-2026-09-30-034: thumbnail_url ''https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Ancient_Xyniai.jpg/400px-Ancient_Xyniai.jpg'' -> ''/data/images/wiki/f9f8e1fa/hero.webp''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:255061", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s022: period_name None -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:255062", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-04_fields-wd3-s022: period_start None -> ''-800''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:354442", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s010: period_name ''1500 - 500 BC'' -> ''Undated''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:354443", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-10-17a_fields-wd5-s010: period_start ''-800'' -> None"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:401983", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_name ''Undated'' -> ''1500 - 500 BC''"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:401984", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "2026-11-07c_mechanical-period-fix-s004: period_start None -> ''-1500''"}]'::jsonb),
