    ('fc247379-6a08-4cca-bd66-ff2c661e6c00'::uuid, 'mystery', '5', '2', 'card-stats-2026-11-07c-rollback:fc247379-6a08-4cca-bd66-ff2c661e6c00:mystery', 'rollback of card-stats-2026-11-07c: mystery ''2'' restored on Lesingey Round', 'de04937bd62d138a31a75a6adf04ce09', '[{"source": "api/cardgame/generator.py:site_card_stats", "url": "api/cardgame/generator.py", "quote": "mystery = 5 from (''Fortress/citadel'', ''Undated'') is shared by 27 curated site(s)"}, {"source": "production export 80b2b77ea294dfe0 (2026-11-07 13:29:26.934212+00)", "url": "remediation_change_log + unified_sites + card_stats (read-only)", "quote": "counterfactual: 766 journalled input value(s) put back reproduce the stored card_stats in all 59556 cells (basis: wave 2026-11-07''s own export (2026-11-07 10:00:39.847916+00))"}, {"source": "remediation_change_log:88596", "url": "remediation_change_log", "quote": "phase4:p4-2205:chunk-0001: description \"Located 1.6 km west of Penzance, Cornwall, Lesingey Round is a ringfort (a smaller hillfort) dating from the late Iron Age to the early post-Roman period (1st century BC – 7th century AD) [1]. It is a ''round'' – the Cornish term for a small circular embanked enclosure with a single entrance, common throughout Cornwall [1]. The site sits at the summit of a wooded hill and features a circular bank measuring 3.7–4.6 metres in width [1]. As a scheduled monument, it represents an important example of defensive settlement architecture from late prehistoric into early medieval Cornwall [1].\" -> ''Lesingey Round is a ringfort, a smaller type of hillfort, about 1 mile west of Penzance, in Cornwall [1]. It is a scheduled monument [1]. Lesingey Round is situated at the summit of a hill [1]. The circular bank is 12–15 feet above the partly buried external ditch and about 6 feet above the interior; it encloses an area of about 1.5 acres [1]. As the inner slope of the rampart is absent in places, the location of the entrance is not known [1]. There are no visible 